{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar","id":971950,"title":"The Role of the Lunar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-18T08:58:16-07:00","id":971950,"title":"The Role of the Lunar","content":"I have been looking at the homebrew lunar stuff and looking again at the things the devs have said about lunars has been saying about them. Problems with themes and how they we do before.<br /> One thing I have seen is people having problems defining them and giving them a role in creation (especially for people who were not really into them and didn\u2019t by their books).<br /> <br /> I think the problem is the other exalted for one.<br /> Solars-rulers, god kings of creation. They represent perfection.<br /> Sidereal- advisers and teachers of the exalted. They guide the world fate in the background<br /> Dragon Blooded- Soldiers of creation. They control the elements them self.<br /> <br /> In the 2nd age the roles of the solars is the reclaim the world and make it better, Sidereals haven\u2019t changed too much just that they work much more in the shadows. And the dragon blooded now control the world (well as much as they can).<br /> <br /> What does this have to do with Lunars? They never <b>had </b>a role hard coded in them. Their role is whatever they want to be, what is needed for them to be. A comment from one of the devs said to truly understand the lunars and run a good game is to understand the setting. I think that is true, they change, adapt. In the 2nd age they are infiltrator that corrupt and cause wars and terrorist that rips power from the realm. They <b>can </b>be anything else too. Just that they happen to be the enemy of the &quot;civilised world&quot;, so it the path of least resistance to use guerrilla tactics when their enemy can track them through fate.<br /> <br /> I myself am a jack of all trades and understand the power of it. I great at managing a project as I can translate between people of different skills and understand each part of the project. My friend started getting film and started a short film, I started out as an actor and ended up co-directing it (partly because I had more experience with film and do it before). I helped the camera men understand what my friend wanted from them as I understand cinematography and recorded film myself. I helped my friend in script writing, especially story boarding understanding how certain shots was be too had to film or work better. Now I wasn\u2019t as good as anyone there in their skills but I could fill in or get them to work together as I have done the roles before (expect my friend who movie this was, it was her first project). But I was really helpful to everyone.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what a lunar does. They can fill a whole missing. That advantage of a hole an enemy has. They will range attack a melee fighter and melee fight and range fighter. <b>Using mostly the same charms. </b>They can't fight a solar sword vs. sword, so why would they? If a sidereal can see through any lie they smash them with the truth.<br /> Think about with Dex 5 and an excellency they have 10 dice to any Dex roll. Crafting, combat, athletics, stealth and so on. They can do a lot of thing epically well <b>without </b>the skill. Being able to have 10 dice to any combat roll with only having Dex 5 is pretty cool compared to a solar with dex 5 perennially having 5-20 dice (yeah I know you could make a dawn with 5 in all weapon skills spending 10 bp to raise to 5, but I\u2019m sure a lunar could do the same as well). My point is it is not hard for a lunar to be good at something, not the best but good. Getting 9 excellencies is something a starting lunar I believe will be able to do to be able an attempt anything.<br /> <br /> tl:dr<br /> Lunars role in creation is what they what it to be.<br /> Lunars role in creation is what is needed of them.<br /> Lunars role in creation is influence by the state of creation<br /> Lunars in the first age helped by filling the holes a Solar or a circle have by being a jack of all trades able to adapt to situation.<br /> Their power comes from not being locked into a certain skill<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br /> Sorry for the length","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:13:10-07:00","id":972023,"title":"","content":"I think you're grokking their Excellency exactly right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:28:42-07:00","id":972128,"title":"","content":"Not just Excellencies but charm too. They will I believe will be used for many different skills","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:49:37-07:00","id":972292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-State</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar#post971950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I myself am a jack of all trades and understand the power of it. I great at managing a project as I can translate between people of different skills and understand each part of the project. My friend started getting film and started a short film, I started out as an actor and ended up co-directing it (partly because I had more experience with film and do it before). I helped the camera men understand what my friend wanted from them as I understand cinematography and recorded film myself. I helped my friend in script writing, especially story boarding understanding how certain shots was be too had to film or work better. Now I wasn\u2019t as good as anyone there in their skills but I could fill in or get them to work together as I have done the roles before (expect my friend who movie this was, it was her first project). But I was really helpful to everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Reminds of that quote from <i>Fantastic Mr Fox</i>: &quot;Listen, you're Kylie. You're an unbelievably nice guy. Your job is really, just to...be available, I think.&quot; There's no such thing as too much help.<br /> <br /> But I still feel like 3E's take on the Lunars was a copout. 'We can't decide what Lunars are so we decided that neither can they! That's their plot arc!' Which doesn't exactly inspire a player, especially compared to the Factions' or the Cult's multiple plot hooks. It sounded to me like Lunars have to be built around the players' group and have no base for an agenda of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:51:41-07:00","id":972317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=972292#post972292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good. Reminds of that quote from <i>Fantastic Mr Fox</i>: &quot;Listen, you're Kylie. You're an unbelievably nice guy. Your job is really, just to...be available, I think.&quot; There's no such thing as too much help.<br /> <br /> But I still feel like 3E's take on the Lunars was a copout. 'We can't decide what Lunars are so we decided that neither can they! That's their plot arc!' Which doesn't exactly inspire a player, especially compared to the Factions' or the Cult's multiple plot hooks. It sounded to me like Lunars have to be built around the players' group and have no base for an agenda of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is something that the Lunars were and what they remain, from what Holden wrote about their roles, but for whatever reason, people didn't take the &quot;werewolf&quot; addition to &quot;noble, seer, soldier&quot; very well. Personally, I love it! It's like the promise of enjoying W:tA without huge portions of the baggage, and being able to make the Mage analogs shut the fuck up no matter how much prep time they have! (^VVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:55:21-07:00","id":972701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=972317#post972317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is something that the Lunars were and what they remain, from what Holden wrote about their roles, but for whatever reason, people didn't take the &quot;werewolf&quot; addition to &quot;noble, seer, soldier&quot; very well. Personally, I love it! It's like the promise of enjoying W:tA without huge portions of the baggage, and being able to make the Mage analogs shut the fuck up no matter how much prep time they have! (^VVVVV^)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since the Mage analogs are Sidereals, they'll be able to make the Werewolf analogs shut up too.<br /> <br /> Which is of course why they're waging a shadow war against each other, using tribes and kingdoms as their soldiers. Jesus fuck, I may like Mage but damn the Lunars are cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:33:51-07:00","id":972726,"title":"","content":"The things I think about Lunars being a Jack-of-All-Trades are:<br /> <br /> 1) I feel like it's something a player who wanted to build a Solar that way could do with a Solar, and get a stronger character at it. Not that characters can't overlap, but I feel like there should be more Lunars have going on than that.<br /> <br /> 2) If you're playing an all Lunar party of 3-5 characters, then what's it like having 5 Jack-of-All-Trades? Is it fun?<br /> <br /> It seems great for the one Lunar with a circle of Solars, and the player likes having a bit of shapeshifting and being a Were-X as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:57:45-07:00","id":972750,"title":"","content":"In my experience, Lunars work fine in groups. Honestly, in some ways they work better than Solar parties.<br /> If the 3rd ed Lunars book was out, I'd probably choose running an all-Lunar game over an all-Solar game.<br /> <br /> Everyone can do most parts of the game at least okay, everyone can sneak into places together, everyone can fly long distances together.<br /> <br /> Lunars are not jack-of-all-trades entirely; they still specialise, just less than Solars do.<br /> <br /> <br /> But anyhow. That's a mechanical role, like how DBs are the teamwork guys and Sidereals are the MA guys and Abyssals are the best necromancers.<br /> <br /> Jack-of-all-trades isn't really much of a &quot;role&quot; in the world.<br /> But honestly? I don't care. Because it's not that important.<br /> I don't think the important thing about Solars is really that they used to be the leaders, it's that they're a)very powerful, and b)can support any human-based character concept. Nor is the important thing about Dragonblood that they used to be the soldiers of the Exalted; it's that they have cool elemental powers, and are less powerful than other Exalts.<br /> <br /> Lunars thing is that they're bestial shapeshifting god-monster anti-heroes. If you want a theme for Lunars, don't look at their mechanical role. The mechanical role should come at the point of design once their themes have already been decided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:09:01-07:00","id":972829,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: The following post is merely my opinion and reaction to the role/concept of Lunars, and am not attempting to prove anyone right or wrong on any given point.<br /> <br /> The issue <i><b>I</b></i> always had with Lunars was the heavy handed reliance on Werewolf &quot;translations&quot; which even went so far as to include Rage. When the splat book came out for 2E I was both deeply disappointed and annoyed with the (IMHO) convoluted and outright broken charms/systems/themes they put to print. <br /> <br /> The <b><i>role</i></b> of Lunars was supposed to be the thematic right hand of Solars, their truest of companions in spirit as well as function. Yet what we got was &quot;rage against Creation and the former injustices of our slave masters!&quot;. It was a severe disconnect for me that left me with the image of a exhausted staff of writers sprawled exhausted around a pool table, piles dead cans of Monster around them, and one of them said &quot;To hell with it, let's just make them fantasy werewolves, rehash, spin, done. yay.&quot;. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T18:19:07-07:00","id":972856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker1728</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=972829#post972829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disclaimer: The following post is merely my opinion and reaction to the role/concept of Lunars, and am not attempting to prove anyone right or wrong on any given point.<br /> <br /> The issue <i><b>I</b></i> always had with Lunars was the heavy handed reliance on Werewolf &quot;translations&quot; which even went so far as to include Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Renown? Because, thus far, nothing so focusing on conflict as Rage has been reproduced, but there sure was an irritating and overly-involved tradition of getting ideological barbarian points in 1e, and it, indeed, made no sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the splat book came out for 2E I was both deeply disappointed and annoyed with the (IMHO) convoluted and outright broken charms/systems/themes they put to print.<br /> <br /> The <b><i>role</i></b> of Lunars was supposed to be the thematic right hand of Solars, their truest of companions in spirit as well as function. Yet what we got was &quot;rage against Creation and the former injustices of our slave masters!&quot;. It was a severe disconnect for me that left me with the image of a exhausted staff of writers sprawled exhausted around a pool table, piles dead cans of Monster around them, and one of them said &quot;To hell with it, let's just make them fantasy werewolves, rehash, spin, done. yay.&quot;.<br /> </div> </div> </div>We are 0 for 2, on the Lunars, not counting EX3, yes. No one listed on the MoEP:Lunars writing credits ever contributed to W:tA, though, and it seems like they went out of their way to distance 2nd edition Lunars from them, what with how the Charms were super-generic, the Knacks had no focus on what type of shapeshifter Lunars were supposed to be, and how chimerae were addressed. DBT was a footnote, RLF was the worst idea ever right down to the concept (but some of it could have worked as an in-born power), and everything that allowed Lunars to compete so distanced themselves from werewolves that you'd be hard pressed to really see them as such when they were hiding as a plant, a need fire, or a land feature that slowly followed you around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T01:37:43-07:00","id":972998,"title":"","content":"I think the Werewolf stuff was more the fluff of their society than the mechanics, with their Renown and the laws of the Silver Pact and so on. But I'm 100% sure those'll be radically different this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:06:53-07:00","id":973046,"title":"","content":"The main thing I think Lunars need is a Silver Pact that's worth being a part of.<br /> The most important thing a Sidereal brings to the table is their relationship with Yu-Shan and the other Sidereals while I find a lot of Lunars would rather pretend the others don't exist which leads to them being more directly compared to the Solars and their returned god-king with no support network schtick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:46:24-07:00","id":973135,"title":"","content":"I suppose this touches on what I always had most trouble wrapping my head around with lunars. The best way I can put it is in terms of the first age.<br /> The solars part in the first age was being the best. They were the cherry on top of all the amazing stuff. Sure any exalt could fight off a fair folk invasion, but solars could do it better. Sure any exalt could help advance and protect society, but solars could do it best.<br /> The dragon blooded role was basically to fill everything in. Mighty as the celestial exalted are, there are far more problems that require the attention of an exalt then there are exalts around to actually solve them. The DBs change that. Now every single city can have an exalted officer solving crimes, an exalted teacher helping to preserve and pass on knowledge.<br /> The sidereal role was to use foresight to make things run smoother. They are the only ones who can use the loom of fate. They can use it to gather knowledge about the past and future very well, as well as to manipulate events to go how they want them. Their native charms do both those things quite well to. Using those powers they can essentially organize and advise the exalts so that the tasks they have go easier.<br /> In all these cases, losing the exalt type would lessen the first age. Lose the solars and you lose the best and brightest responsible for the greater parts of the first age. Lose the sidereals and you lose important foresight and have to dedicate more manpower to solving problems as they come up that you would have known about before. Lose the dragon blooded and you lose the hundreds of thousands of men and women who could manage the hundreds of thousands of individual threats across creation.<br /> But what did the lunars do? What role does they play that fell on them alone? Sure they can shapeshifted, but in the grand scheme of things that's simply a means to an end. There didn't appear to me to be anything that lunars could do that the others couldn't. It seemed that if you lost lunars, besides the decrease in raw manpower from losing a bunch of celestial exalts, the first age wouldn't have been really affected.<br /> This thread has been a little helpful though, and I'm interested in seeing where the devs take lunars as the edition unfolds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:53:08-07:00","id":973138,"title":"","content":"I've seen people(in chats elsewhere) griping that Lunars don't have a set role to play in the setting. And it boggles my mind that people want to lock down the most adapable splat into a concrete role. I think their role is to adapt to the situation, where all the other Exalts(even Solars in their unstoppable-train-coming-through-choo-choo way) have to come at the situation in a way that makes it adapt to them(or they just fail at it).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:53:40-07:00","id":973906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=972856#post972856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Charms were super-generic</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually <i>not </i>because of Werewolf, but because of the Eclipse Charmshare effect and the fact that the write didn't want Solars to be able to shapeshift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:04:51-07:00","id":973911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973906#post973906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually <i>not </i>because of Werewolf, but because of the Eclipse Charmshare effect and the fact that the write didn't want Solars to be able to shapeshift.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still leaves 2/3 of the listed problems or possibly more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:20:06-07:00","id":973919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973138#post973138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen people(in chats elsewhere) griping that Lunars don't have a set role to play in the setting. And it boggles my mind that people want to lock down the most adapable splat into a concrete role. I think their role is to adapt to the situation, where all the other Exalts(even Solars in their unstoppable-train-coming-through-choo-choo way) have to come at the situation in a way that makes it adapt to them(or they just fail at it).</div> </div> </div> </div> I can sort of see why, 2e did push the roles the Exalts were originally intended to serve in a way that left Lunars feeling like an odd duck. The problem was that these roles weren't necessarily good for the Exalts in question, Dragon-Blooded got this sudden and unpleasant push toward cannon fodder and Abyssals... where do I fucking start with Abyssals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:55:28-07:00","id":973958,"title":"","content":"Mechanical flexibility doesn't have to mean SETTING flexibility. As I understand it, Exalts were made for a purpose, with the different kinds serving different roles-- soldiers, kings, spies, etc. But Lunars... as a relatively new player, I don't know where they fit into that. Why were they originally created? What role were they meant to play after the Primordials were dealt with? &quot;Whatever was necessary in that moment&quot; doesn't feel like a great answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:08:29-07:00","id":973964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973958#post973958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Whatever was necessary in that moment&quot; doesn't feel like a great answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were made to support the Solars, who are focused specialists until much later in their development. And what does a specialist need the most? Someone to support them where they are weak. And in the Storyteller system, that's a lot of abilities that they need help with. Enter the Attribute-focused Lunars. Lunars can, via their Attribute Excellencies, boost their capabilities over a wide range of abilities. Then you figure in the shapeshifting that allows them to forms to instaboost specific areas(like a bird for mobility, a tyrant lizard for demolitions, DBT for combat, etc) and it seems painfully apparent to me that Lunars have the capability to back up that allpurpose support role, before you even get into their Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:49:24-07:00","id":973986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973964#post973964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were made to support the Solars, who are focused specialists until much later in their development. And what does a specialist need the most? Someone to support them where they are weak. And in the Storyteller system, that's a lot of abilities that they need help with. Enter the Attribute-focused Lunars. Lunars can, via their Attribute Excellencies, boost their capabilities over a wide range of abilities. Then you figure in the shapeshifting that allows them to forms to instaboost specific areas(like a bird for mobility, a tyrant lizard for demolitions, DBT for combat, etc) and it seems painfully apparent to me that Lunars have the capability to back up that allpurpose support role, before you even get into their Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a mechanical role, though, not an in-universe one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:35:22-07:00","id":974003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973958#post973958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanical flexibility doesn't have to mean SETTING flexibility. As I understand it, Exalts were made for a purpose, with the different kinds serving different roles-- soldiers, kings, spies, etc. But Lunars... as a relatively new player, I don't know where they fit into that. Why were they originally created? What role were they meant to play after the Primordials were dealt with? &quot;Whatever was necessary in that moment&quot; doesn't feel like a great answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were created to kick ass and take forms. When fighting a desperate war, I don't think you need to design everything for a specific role after the war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:47:46-07:00","id":974010,"title":"","content":"I can see a couple different possible 'roles' for the Lunar, both based on their mechanical function (i.e. what they were 'designed' to be capable of) and the personality of their patron.<br /> <br /> 1: The Guardians of Creation. Like Luna and his/her/its/whatevers deep and enduring love for Gaia (and deep love for trolling/devastating the Fair Folk)...the Lunars were created to safeguard Creation. The Solars were intended to rule, to lead--The Sidereals to advise--and the Lunars to protect. They were intended to be out in the world, using their unique capabilities to blend in...to go where no one else could...and to crush the enemies of Creation wherever they might be.<br /> <br /> Honestly, this one feels a little narratively weak to me, because technically all of the Exalted are intended to protect Creation...but it's an interpretation I've seen before.<br /> <br /> 2: The &quot;Bottom-Up&quot; equivalent to the Solars' &quot;Top-Down&quot; approach. Solars lead from the front...larger than life heroes that say &quot;Follow Me!&quot; and don't need to look back to make sure you are coming. Lunars lead from within...they mix into the crowd and say &quot;Come on, you can do this,&quot; and inspire action from those around them.<br /> <br /> Again, this one feels a bit weak, because it pigeonholes Lunars quite a lot...though I do like how it has the sort of 'counterpart' feel that Luna and Sol already share.<br /> <br /> 3: A balance to the Solars. A Lunar may not be able to match a Solar power for power...but they are (or rather, should be) adaptable enough to stand against them anyway if the need arose. The Solars draw on the Perfection of the Sun. The problem is that this can distance them from their humanity, even without the Great Curse. Lunars also run the risk of distancing themselves from humanity...but have a tendency to go in the opposite direction...towards the feral, instinctive side. And besides that...Lunars know exactly what it is like to hit rock bottom, they know what it's like to suffer and want to give in...because that is exactly where they were then Luna came to them. Solars may not have had such an experience...their Exaltation likely occurred during one of their finest moments as a mortal and (barring the Great Curse, which wasn't in the plan when they were designed) it basically would have been constantly getting better from there, and thus have a harder time relating to it...something the Lunars would give them.<br /> <br /> Still doesn't feel quite like a definite 'role,' honestly.<br /> <br /> 4: &quot;I don't know, dammit, figure out your own destiny...I gave you all the tools you need.&quot;<br /> <br /> This....sounds a lot like Luna, actually. Luna is very big on freedom, endurance, and forging your own path. It honestly wouldn't surprise me if Luna <i>didn't</i> pick out some concrete 'role' for her chosen and, instead, was like &quot;Here, I gave you a Swiss Army Knife set of powers...use them as you best see fit!&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, of these so far...I'm liking #4, with perhaps a few glimmers of the other ones stuck in as the sorts of things Lunars 'tended' to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3937,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","user":"guildsbounty","date":". 09-21-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T19:36:09-07:00","id":974190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guildsbounty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974010#post974010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4: &quot;I don't know, dammit, figure out your own destiny...I gave you all the tools you need.&quot;<br /> <br /> This....sounds a lot like Luna, actually. Luna is very big on freedom, endurance, and forging your own path. It honestly wouldn't surprise me if Luna <i>didn't</i> pick out some concrete 'role' for her chosen and, instead, was like &quot;Here, I gave you a Swiss Army Knife set of powers...use them as you best see fit!&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, of these so far...I'm liking #4, with perhaps a few glimmers of the other ones stuck in as the sorts of things Lunars 'tended' to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, it's one thing for the <i>Lunars </i>to take this approach, but another when the <i>players and ST </i>can't figure out what the hell a Lunar campaign is supposed to be. And even then, Solars already occupy the playspace of &quot;anything you could possibly want to do&quot; - as a matter of personal taste, I wish they didn't, but c'est la vie - and whatever a Solar chooses to do, they will do better than anyone else. Meanwhile, under the setting dictate that the Age of Sorrows be the Age of Sorrows, giving Lunars the role of &quot;I dunno, whatever&quot; relegates them to doing 'whatever' <i>badly</i>, or else there's no reason for the Solars to come in and fix everything. This makes the Lunars look like a bunch of stump-fucking asshole idiots, and likewise tarnishes any of the groups and peoples associated with them in the lore.<br /> <br /> My preferred solution would be to emphasize that meaningful achievement is <i>really fucking hard </i>when very nearly the whole world is against you, and that the Lunars could accomplish a lot more and in a much more positive fashion if they had some breathing room from the Deebs and Sidereals trying to murder them nonstop. This is one reason I keep asking what Lunars do when they're <i>not </i>murdering Sids or Deebs, and what the less-hostile side of their powerset will look like - it's hard to portray a faction that routinely <i>eats people </i>as a matter of course sympathetically, and New Friend Aroma from the sample Changing Moon's list is preeeeeetty skeevy, which might well be the point, but still...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","user":"Thesaurasaurus","date":". 09-21-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T19:46:48-07:00","id":974194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974190#post974190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when very nearly the whole world is against you, and that the Lunars could accomplish a lot more and in a much more positive fashion if they had some breathing room from the Deebs and Sidereals trying to murder them nonstop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boohoo. Lunars at least have established elders for support. Solars can count on nobody, not even each other, so they have to do everything the hard way.<br /> <br /> But that's okay. When all Creation sets their hand against the Solars, that just makes for a good challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T22:53:18-07:00","id":974249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974190#post974190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, it's one thing for the <i>Lunars </i>to take this approach, but another when the <i>players and ST </i>can't figure out what the hell a Lunar campaign is supposed to be. And even then, Solars already occupy the playspace of &quot;anything you could possibly want to do&quot; - as a matter of personal taste, I wish they didn't, but c'est la vie - and whatever a Solar chooses to do, they will do better than anyone else. Meanwhile, under the setting dictate that the Age of Sorrows be the Age of Sorrows, giving Lunars the role of &quot;I dunno, whatever&quot; relegates them to doing 'whatever' <i>badly</i>, or else there's no reason for the Solars to come in and fix everything. This makes the Lunars look like a bunch of stump-fucking asshole idiots, and likewise tarnishes any of the groups and peoples associated with them in the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going off of the &quot;intense emotions&quot; portion of werewolves that WW has made, a Lunar campaign probably involves fierce passion for something, devotion toward it in a big way. By default, it is &quot;fuck the Realm&quot; and involves wrathfully stepping up the process of its takedown. Other options do exist, but you'll have to discover something you feel intensely toward in the setting, and make a character around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My preferred solution would be to emphasize that meaningful achievement is <i>really fucking hard </i>when very nearly the whole world is against you, and that the Lunars could accomplish a lot more and in a much more positive fashion if they had some breathing room from the Deebs and Sidereals trying to murder them nonstop. This is one reason I keep asking what Lunars do when they're <i>not </i>murdering Sids or Deebs, and what the less-hostile side of their powerset will look like - it's hard to portray a faction that routinely <i>eats people </i>as a matter of course sympathetically, and New Friend Aroma from the sample Changing Moon's list is preeeeeetty skeevy, which might well be the point, but still... </div> </div> </div>Where does that extrapolation leave DBs and their social Charms, then? Especially the one that the older DB has that wears away Willpower faster? Because it can go to those same skeevy places at least as quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:32:00-07:00","id":974261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973911#post973911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That still leaves 2/3 of the listed problems or possibly more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I didn't say it was a <i>good</i> thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's just another example of how charmshare ruins everything and that nobody misses it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:30:30-07:00","id":974277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974249#post974249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going off of the &quot;intense emotions&quot; portion of werewolves that WW has made, a Lunar campaign probably involves fierce passion for something, devotion toward it in a big way. By default, it is &quot;fuck the Realm&quot; and involves wrathfully stepping up the process of its takedown. Other options do exist, but you'll have to discover something you feel intensely toward in the setting, and make a character around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the Relentless Lunar Fury/Irresistible Silver Spirit/Inevitable Genius Insight grouping of Charms, but handled in a more interesting and compelling way?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974249#post974249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does that extrapolation leave DBs and their social Charms, then? Especially the one that the older DB has that wears away Willpower faster? Because it can go to those same skeevy places at least as quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Operative word: <b>can</b>. Hopefully the full-text version of NFA will feel less date-rapey, or at least be more emphatic that using it to get sex is rape, no seriously, chemically-induced, overpowering lust does NOT allow for informed consent. Grinding Millstone Argument <i>can </i>be used to badger your way into bed, but that isn't manifestly the default use, so if someone does take it in that direction it's clearly on them, not the Charm excusing them for &quot;just playing their character&quot; by RAW. Similarly, I really hope that Warm-Faced Seduction Style doesn't make a return.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T01:39:39-07:00","id":974295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, it's one thing for the <i>Lunars </i>to take this approach, but another when the <i>players and ST </i>can't figure out what the hell a Lunar campaign is supposed to be. </div> </div> </div>How is doing a Lunar campaign any harder than a Solar campaign? People do that all the time.<br /> <br /> Almost every type of campaign you'd do with Solars, you can do with Lunars (though at a slightly lower power level). You're more likely to have a campaign that involves barbarians and wyld mutants and Raksha, but that's purely stylistic. You don't have to.<br /> <br /> Plus, you can also do a similar campaign but with a support network of elders if you wish.<br /> <br /> And of course, you can do a Silver Pact campaign where you're part of a wide military-guerilla campaign to fight the Realm.<br /> <br /> I've played a Lunar campaign before (though not for very long). We made alliances between desert tribes and ended up having a giant battle against a horde of Fair Folk.<br /> Which you could equally do with Solars, except we had a society that bound us together, rather than simply got together because we all glow the same colour.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I think in many ways Lunar campaigns work better than Solar campaigns. If the Lunar book was out, I'd be pretty tempted to run an all-Lunar campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:58:18-07:00","id":974312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973958#post973958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanical flexibility doesn't have to mean SETTING flexibility. As I understand it, Exalts were made for a purpose, with the different kinds serving different roles-- soldiers, kings, spies, etc. But Lunars... as a relatively new player, I don't know where they fit into that. Why were they originally created? What role were they meant to play after the Primordials were dealt with? &quot;Whatever was necessary in that moment&quot; doesn't feel like a great answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we should care too much about the specific roles the Incarnae had in mind for their Chosen. At its core, Exalted is a game about human agency, choices and consequences, with the god-granted powers of the Chosen acting as a magnifying lens for human power, ambition and hubris. What the gods who created Exalted had in mind for their champions is largely irrelevant to the themes of the game, except in the context of the Exalted Host transcending the gods' plans and forging new roles for themselves as they saw fit - the question at the core of the game is what <b>you</b> will do with the power you have.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that some people are really struggling to grasp the peculiar place the gods take in Exalted, and start treating these supposed original roles of the Exalted as some perfected celestial hierarchy which must be restored at all cost if Creation is to thrive again. This is largely an extension of the 2e's fixation on the First Age and how everything that isn't exactly like First Age must be utter shit, but this part in particular had been historically used by people to justify some truly horrible, inhumane and plain distasteful shit which I'd rather not see ever again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","user":"Morangias","date":"and other clever-sounding words. 09-22-2016, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T03:43:07-07:00","id":974325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974312#post974312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we should care too much about the specific roles the Incarnae had in mind for their Chosen. At its core, Exalted is a game about human agency, choices and consequences, with the god-granted powers of the Chosen acting as a magnifying lens for human power, ambition and hubris. What the gods who created Exalted had in mind for their champions is largely irrelevant to the themes of the game, except in the context of the Exalted Host transcending the gods' plans and forging new roles for themselves as they saw fit - the question at the core of the game is what <b>you</b> will do with the power you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I've been trying to say, but you've said it better.<br /> <br /> The first step of Exalted splats is &quot;Solars let you play really powerful but still human-esque heroes, Dragon-blood let you play aristocratic elemental heroes, Lunars let you play bestial god-monster heroes, Sidereals let you play Secret Old Kung-Fu Masters, etc&quot;.<br /> <br /> The &quot;what is this Exalt for&quot; is a setting justification made up later to give the splat some backstory.<br /> <br /> The writers should be going &quot;Lunars are awesome bestial god-monster heroes who steal faces and turn into badass beats of legend!...<br /> I guess we should come up with a reason the Gods made them. Uh, because that's what you get when Luna makes Exalts I guess? Or maybe it was useful to take on bestial demon-monsters by becoming badass monsters too? Or something?&quot;<br /> <br /> Rather than &quot;Lunars were made to, uh, be jack-of-all-trades I guess? To cover the holes other Exalts didn't cover and adapt to whatever Third-Circle Demon they were fighting that day? So, how can we make a splat with powers based on that? I guess, make kind of good at everything but not really good at anything?&quot;<br /> That's really the wrong way to design them.<br /> <br /> People should pick up the Lunar book and go &quot;Wow Lunars are really cool! I want to play a Lunar so I can play a bestial anti-hero who steals the face of a Dragonblood's servant and then sneaks into his room and turns into a giant bear-monster and mauls his face off! That'll be awesome!&quot;<br /> Or, alternatively, &quot;I enjoy problem-solving by having a toolbox of different forms and working out how to leverage them to solve particular problems, rather than just rolling a bucket of dice at them, and Lunar mechanics seem to do this, but in a less wacky way than Sidereal mechanics.&quot;<br /> Or, alternatively, &quot;I want to play a champion of the barbarian peoples who takes the form of their patron animal to lead them to victory.&quot;<br /> Or even &quot;I want to play a werewolf in this fantasy game. Werewolves are cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because if they pick up the book and go &quot;So, the point of these guys is the gods made them to kind of do a bit of everything because the other Exalts were more specialised?&quot; Well, that's not very inspiring. It's probably going to make you want to play one of these other more interesting-sounding splats, which is a pity, because IMO Lunars are one of the more interesting splats, they've just been written badly both mechanically* and in terms of the fluff (because the game is obsessed with Solars vs Dragonblood/Sidereals vs Abyssals and forgets about the fact that the Solars are the new kids on the block and the Lunars have been fighting the Realm and ruling barbarian kingdoms for 1500 years, then tries to slot Lunars into a setting that's not really designed for them to exist.<br /> But I think the Devs know this, and what they've said about Lunars seems to be generally going on the right track. What they want Lunars to be like seems much better, frankly, than what some &quot;fans&quot; seem to want, which is not actually Lunars at all.)<br /> <br /> *Well, No Moons. Changing Moons and Full Moons weren't perfect, but I wouldn't say they were written worse mechanically than Solars or Abyssals or Dragonblood. Possibly better than Dragonblood. And obviously they were written better mechanically than Sidereals. I'd much rather have run a Lunar game than a Sidereal game, in terms of mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-22-2016, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:03:28-07:00","id":974338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974190#post974190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, it's one thing for the <i>Lunars </i>to take this approach, but another when the <i>players and ST </i>can't figure out what the hell a Lunar campaign is supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's that they can't figure it out but rather that you weren't really encouraged to interact with other Lunars.<br /> <br /> Fluffwise a lot of them were kind of dull* in a way that got drowned out by the likes of Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi.<br /> <br /> Mechanically your benefits of being in the Silver Pact are the tattoos. Aside from that you're in the same boat as a Solar and expected to buy your Mentor and other backgrounds that represent your standing in the Pact and if you don't it's implied you basically just went &quot;thanks for the training and tattoos, smell you later&quot; I like that there's less inherent obligation than being schooled in the Realm or trained by the Bureau of Destiny but there's no incentive to stay. In my experience there were far more people who were inspired by the Solar Bond to play a Lunar in a mixed game because as double edged as it potentially was they could take it to a friend's PC and enjoy some cap busting dice for mixed splat teamwork.<br /> <br /> *I actually think that the Thousand Streams River Project had a lot of potential that was squandered by refusing to see the terrifying implications of having your society secretly directed by skinwalking puppet masters and focusing entirely on how well meaning the Lunars are with these plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-22-2016, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:52:07-07:00","id":974378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974277#post974277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Relentless Lunar Fury/Irresistible Silver Spirit/Inevitable Genius Insight grouping of Charms, but handled in a more interesting and compelling way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. I don't look well upon that trio, though, so I don't try to frame it in any way, shape, or form similar to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Operative word: <b>can</b>. Hopefully the full-text version of NFA will feel less date-rapey, or at least be more emphatic that using it to get sex is rape, no seriously, chemically-induced, overpowering lust does NOT allow for informed consent. Grinding Millstone Argument <i>can </i>be used to badger your way into bed, but that isn't manifestly the default use, so if someone does take it in that direction it's clearly on them, not the Charm excusing them for &quot;just playing their character&quot; by RAW. Similarly, I really hope that Warm-Faced Seduction Style doesn't make a return. </div> </div> </div>Grinding Millstone Argument exists in a manner that makes it incredibly easy to use for terrible, terrible purposes of all kinds, often for bypassing regulations in place for good reason while trying to build up a corrupt power block, when not used to become a PUA. Conversely, New Friend Aroma can make people be, well, your friend. It's right there in the Charm text as the option alternate to sex. Given the existence of the Red Rule, a group might only see the non-sexual versions of both in operation.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't bet on Warm-Faced Seduction Smile being left out. There's not much of a reason for it to be left out of the new edition, given the existence of the Solar seduction Charms. It could be in a more fitting Ability, though, since Socialize never fit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:51:41-07:00","id":974746,"title":"","content":"Lunar Exalted seem to embody the pursuit of freedom and self-identity.<br /> <br /> They are chosen from those who know what it is like to live in captivity, trapped by one thing or another. Unable to live as they would chose. Luna gives them the power to escape and find their own place in the world.<br /> <br /> Further, when they are reborn, she gives each of them a Totem form to reveal their true self. Or perhaps all Lunars now choose their own Totems?<br /> <br /> For sure, Lunar Exalted are the only Host that gets to choose their Caste.<br /> <br /> <br /> Luna isn't the Unconquered Sun; she probably didn't envision her Chosen leading and uniting and elevating humanity into something greater. Luna may just not even care about humanity aside from the individuals she falls in love with and Exalts, which would be a neat reason why the Exalted of the Moon call themselves &quot;Luna's Beloved&quot;. Luna wants to make her loved ones happy, but perhaps doesn't care what they do to find happiness.<br /> <br /> She would certainly prefer that they do something to defend Creation from Fair Folk, the Underworld, and demons, but that's something that most Lunar Exalted -- as human beings who were born and raised in Creation -- are naturally inclined to do, so that works well enough for her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T01:46:59-07:00","id":975883,"title":"","content":"The jack of all trades idea sounds good but it has a problem. Their is very little a Solar can't do. Everything a human can do times eleven is not very limiting. Add the sun stuff and the king over everything stuff and some stuff I'm probably forgetting and you get a very vast list of powers Solars can get access to. Made worst by the fact that the developers often show less restrict when it comes to giving Solars new toys then a child left alone with cake. In short jack of all trades master of non doesn't make Luners stand out against Solars jack of all trades master of all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T02:22:52-07:00","id":975889,"title":"","content":"Well, a 100xp Solar is generally very good at a small number of things, whereas a 100xp Lunar is generally okay at most things.<br /> But you are right, it's hardly inspiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T06:25:08-07:00","id":975923,"title":"","content":"The Solars were made to do the bidding of the Sun, the Lunars for the Moon and the Sidereals for the planets.<br /> <br /> The setting stuff has been fairly good at saying what the Sun wanted his Chosen to do - lead humans, defeat monsters, do great deeds - and what the planets wanted the Sidereals to do - advise humans, work with the gods to design better fates for man, preserve the weave of fate.<br /> <br /> It's been a bit weak on what the Moon wanted the Lunars to do, and IMO, unless it's &quot;Choose for and please yourselves&quot;, which is rather weak, I think it's inevitably going to overlap with the Solar &quot;mission&quot;. Jenna Moran, on the rare occasion(s) she talked about Lunars I think once or twice (which I can't find links for), identified them as &quot;culture heroes&quot;. Which is more a tag that goes with Solars in current meta discussion, but I think it's a bit unavoidable to go to Lunars, as Lunars as totally in isolation from championing and leading or representing cultures and their interests in a sincere way I think doesn't totally work for me. I mean yes you can be your own person, but I think you get more out of it if you go &quot;Look, the Luna made them to guide and lead mankind&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:30:23-07:00","id":976003,"title":"","content":"I don't want to play a Lunar to do things as well as a Solar.<br /> <br /> I want to play a Lunar to do things in the way that only a Lunar can do.<br /> <br /> A Dawn Caste may fight better than a Full Moon, but only the Full Moon could fight by constantly shapeshifting into different animal forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:21:23-07:00","id":977293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974190#post974190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>See, it's one thing for the <i>Lunars </i>to take this approach, but another when the <i>players and ST </i>can't figure out what the hell a Lunar campaign is supposed to be.</b></span> And even then, Solars already occupy the playspace of &quot;anything you could possibly want to do&quot; - as a matter of personal taste, I wish they didn't, but c'est la vie - and whatever a Solar chooses to do, they will do better than anyone else. Meanwhile, under the setting dictate that the Age of Sorrows be the Age of Sorrows, giving Lunars the role of &quot;I dunno, whatever&quot; relegates them to doing 'whatever' <i>badly</i>, or else there's no reason for the Solars to come in and fix everything. This makes the Lunars look like a bunch of stump-fucking asshole idiots, and likewise tarnishes any of the groups and peoples associated with them in the lore.<br /> <br /> My preferred solution would be to emphasize that meaningful achievement is <i>really fucking hard </i>when very nearly the whole world is against you, and that the Lunars could accomplish a lot more and in a much more positive fashion if they had some breathing room from the Deebs and Sidereals trying to murder them nonstop. This is one reason I keep asking what Lunars do when they're <i>not </i>murdering Sids or Deebs, and what the less-hostile side of their powerset will look like - it's hard to portray a faction that routinely <i>eats people </i>as a matter of course sympathetically, and New Friend Aroma from the sample Changing Moon's list is preeeeeetty skeevy, which might well be the point, but still...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what my old group and I had issue with, when sitting around our gaming pit and discussing what campaigns are about, we ran in circles. The fact that Lunars were so highly adaptable and &quot;monster heroes&quot; wasn't the issue, it was what's their theme within the setting? With Solar it was fairly easy, we called it the &quot;Phoenix Effect&quot;, which in brief was rising from the ashes of Creation's tottering on the edge, the Solar rebuild it to a new and glorious 3rd Age with their chief opponent being the Abyssals and Death Lords. <i>(Note: This was my group and I's theme for Solar, not meant to imply this is what the authors of the books were claiming it was or should be).</i><br /> <br /> Running a campaign where Solar and Lunar worked together towards that end was fine, as the Lunar were able to cover 2 or more weak sides of their Solar mate and were their ultimate Lts and ultimately that's what we wound up doing and it was a fairly enjoyable campaign. We had discussed beforehand how in a <i>&quot;Phoenix Effect&quot; </i>campaign, the Lunar was <u><b><i>the one</i></b></u> individual a Solar could truly trust above all others, even more so than their Circle mates whom they had faced against so much with. But a Lunar only campaign left us feeling that it was too much like a Werewolf campaign, not due to mechanical systems but due to the society the splat painted, what with the Elders, Silver Path, etc. We also discussed how Lunar don't have their version of Abyssals and why that was, but that is a different rabbit hole altogether and again, showed plenty of &quot;crossing the proton streams&quot; (obscure Ghostbuster's reference) of W;tA and EX.<br /> <br /> Now part of the blame rests with us as gamers, who were devoted fans of the ST system (even though I often had to spend 100s of hours creating houseruled rewrites) as we had a lot of material stuck in our heads from other WW products as well as time played. Thus while the staff who wrote the Lunar book may not have contributed to any W:tA material, they (the Lunar authors) were likely affected to a certain extent just like we were, given how so many people who purchased/read the Lunar book drew many of the same comparisons my group and I did.<br /> <br /> Later, back when my days didn't shrink to next to no free time, I did a Lunar rewrite that I shared with some other STs whom I met with online and did a bit of collaborating with. Unfortunately, several computer upgrades and hard-drive shreddings later, that rewrite is no longer to be found in either my archives or those I shared it with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Its summed up behind the spoiler below sparing casual readers my meandering babble.<br /> <br /> (Disclaimer: Below is my solution that suited my intentions and goals for Lunar, it is not meant to imply it was superior to canon text or other people's ideas).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I had decided that what had me stumped as a ST was the thematic pairing of Sun and Moon as &quot;a couple&quot; when the text clearly suggested that Luna adored Gaia, but deferred to the US as It's lord that It <i>had</i> to obey (as did every other deity in creation) and was reinforced by the mating of Lunars to Solar. This is where I decided my rewrite needed to take place, so instead I said that Luna was an<i> ally that the US courted</i> and convinced to join the cause by his agreeing that Gaia was to be not only spared, but protected and nurtured.<br /> <br /> I felt that the US ruled the day, and Luna the night, and much as in several classic myths the two &quot;shared dominion and duties of the sky&quot;. Thus Luna is treated as a equal had It's own chosen, who would also commit to being allies to the US's chosen. This alliance was a bond the two parties would simply be able to sense and each would shore up the other's weaknesses much as their patrons did. There was no inherit slavery or obedience in this bond, it was instinctual level of &quot;understanding/knowing&quot; of each other with both generally sharing the greater goal of protecting and nurturing of Creation aka Gaia (note that Solar and Lunar differed in opinion as to what that meant when it came time to discuss details, but they were of the same mind when it came to the larger picture).<br /> <br /> Then I decided that the Solar and Lunar each had a &quot;impeccable foe&quot; that they were ideally suited to fight, Creation had two primary enemies: The Primordials and The Wyld. These were two separate threats that required different kinds of champions, so the Solar were <i>more</i> suited to combat the Primordials and their ilk, and the Lunars were <i>more</i> suited to fight the Wyld. The word &quot;more&quot; is deliberate, while Lunars could fight Yozi and what not, their natural enemy was The Wyld and were innately more suited dealing with its chaotic energies than the Solar were, but that didn't mean Solar couldn't/didn't fight Fae or Lunar didn't fight Yozi, it just meant one was natural assets within easier reach to combat their primary foes with.<br /> <br /> I had always cast my EX games as a &quot;Flat Earth&quot; style universe, where Creation was a disk floating in a sea of chaos, the edge of Creation came into contact with The Wyld where due to that contact, the Wyld had the most amount of defined form while still being &quot;of chaos&quot;, but the deeper into &quot;the disk&quot; elements of the Wyld reached, the more beholden to the rules of existence such creatures became and the more defined. Thus a Fae well within Creation became a unique, but fixed, entity of finite abilities and (often strange) ritual, manners, alliances, etc. The &quot;edges&quot; of Creation were in a state of constant flux, the greater the empires of the Solar became, the larger Creation became. The Solar brought order and stability, as their domains grew, Creation expanded. In other words, the world disk got bigger in direct proportion to the efforts of the Solar as they grew the height of the first age.<br /> <br /> The Lunar patrolled/guarded against the Wyld, though the greater share of this activity was at the outer third of Creation's borders, their duties would frequently draw them well within the inner 2/3rds of Creation (as &quot;measured&quot; out from the Earth pole). They would assist their Solar allies as needed, and frequently worked together towards common goals as they would lend each other's might against one another's &quot;natural&quot; enemies. So in a way, they were 'co-rulers' of Creation, in manner similar to how Luna and the US ruled the sky.<br /> <br /> When the Uprising took place, it was a act of betrayal against the Lunar as much as it was the Solar, it wasn't a case of the Lunars saying &quot;The Sidereal and Terrestrials betrayed my Lord and Master&quot; as it was a case of &quot;The Sidereal and Terrestrials betrayed Creation <i>and us</i>&quot;. The Lunar still have their natural foe of the Wyld, they are the ones who keep the Wyld from consuming Creation but they have lost much ground (as the decline of the Shogunate shows) over the years and were stretched too thin to combat the likes of the Death Lords, Yozi, Fae, and the general disarray of Heaven, at least until the Solar started to come back. So if anything, the Lunar are letting out a (cautious) sigh of relief and feel like their <i>allies</i> and companions of times past, have finally managed to find their way back.<br /> <br /> Thus the elder Lunar don't have this entire outlook of former slaves having seen in the aftermath the reality of their collars, because that was never the case. However they did notice that the Solar had at the height of their abilities, enslaved lives of lesser power which led to the Usurpation. This makes the elders regard the new Solar with caution, while they may not know of the Great Curse per say, they do know that the Solar are not without flaws and can fall prey to excess, much like civilized nations can justify excesses in the name of a good cause. That doesn't mean they forgive those who endorsed the Usurpation, far from it, for to them all of the Exalted were part of a sacred oath that had been broken. Those who hold to the ideals behind the Usurpation are their enemies only slightly less than the Wyld/Primordials are. But those who fight against the Usurpation are seen as allies, be they DB or Sidereal.<br /> <br /> So a all Lunar's theme was about assisting the Solar from time to time, delivering a unholy smackdown on those who &quot;believe in the Usurpation&quot; (that belief loosely stated says both the US and Luna are not to be worshiped/respected and are replaced with the DBs and little gods as the lords of Creation), keep the Wyld and its minions at bay, and fight against anything that &quot;threatens Gaia&quot; (i.e. Creation as a concept of ordered reality, of which the Natural Order is part of).<br /> <br /> The snag I hit was with power levels. Conceptually I felt Solar and Lunars were equal in power, but the charms were already enough of a head ache and each had plenty of abusive loop holes they could exploit to where the only thing that I really had to debate was whether or not Lunar could do Solar level Sorcery. For my games i decided that they could, but their Sorcery was only capable of such heights with the proper phase of the moon. Loosely put, you want to do &quot;War Solar Sorcery&quot; it had to be on the nights of the full moon, etc. Otherwise I figured the differences in their charms didn't point at one innately being able to beat the other if they had the same degree of development, but I might've been wrong on that as I never had a chance to experiment with it.<br /> <br /> I also did away with the 5 castes to mirror 5 castes things, but I don't recall at this moment all the things I did there, only that I had simplified it to the Full/Half/No moons and the Casteless were a type of Lunar who had no Solar ally and could venture deeper into the Wyld than other Lunar. I had also created a type of Solar that ironically enough, Onyx represented better as Exigents, but who at the time had no Lunar ally and didn't quite fall into any of the 5 Solar Castes.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":12415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","user":"Seeker1728","date":".  edited for clarity as writing post was interrupted. 09-27-2016, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:24:19-07:00","id":977340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=972292#post972292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good. Reminds of that quote from <i>Fantastic Mr Fox</i>: &quot;Listen, you're Kylie. You're an unbelievably nice guy. Your job is really, just to...be available, I think.&quot; There's no such thing as too much help.<br /> <br /> But I still feel like 3E's take on the Lunars was a copout. 'We can't decide what Lunars are so we decided that neither can they! That's their plot arc!' Which doesn't exactly inspire a player, especially compared to the Factions' or the Cult's multiple plot hooks. It sounded to me like Lunars have to be built around the players' group and have no base for an agenda of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't feel like we've actually gotten 3e's take on Lunars yet. Not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:29:16-07:00","id":977344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973958#post973958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanical flexibility doesn't have to mean SETTING flexibility. As I understand it, Exalts were made for a purpose, with the different kinds serving different roles-- soldiers, kings, spies, etc. But Lunars... as a relatively new player, I don't know where they fit into that. Why were they originally created? What role were they meant to play after the Primordials were dealt with? &quot;Whatever was necessary in that moment&quot; doesn't feel like a great answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not new, they were there for the Primordial War and everything. Also, they weren't &quot;designed&quot; per se, they were given the blessings and powers of the Moon, just like Solars were given the blessings and powers of the Sun. However that worked, I'm pretty sure engineering design documents weren't involved. <br /> <br /> (Yes, even on Autochthon's end. He honestly seems more like Tesla to me, who was famous for his ability to just build stuff that works without notes or anything, because he could just do it all in his head.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:13:29-07:00","id":977386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=977344#post977344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Yes, even on Autochthon's end. He honestly seems more like Tesla to me, who was famous for his ability to just build stuff that works without notes or anything, because he could just do it all in his head.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting comparison, actually made me like Autochthon more for thinking of it that way. May have to reread that splat book now when i get the time. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T03:55:59-07:00","id":978302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=972726#post972726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The things I think about Lunars being a Jack-of-All-Trades are:<br /> <br /> 1) I feel like it's something a player who wanted to build a Solar that way could do with a Solar, and get a stronger character at it. Not that characters can't overlap, but I feel like there should be more Lunars have going on than that.<br /> <br /> 2) If you're playing an all Lunar party of 3-5 characters, then what's it like having 5 Jack-of-All-Trades? Is it fun?<br /> <br /> It seems great for the one Lunar with a circle of Solars, and the player likes having a bit of shapeshifting and being a Were-X as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) A Full moon meele lunar in a fight could add most of his charms to a bow or his fist/claws/etc. Lets say lunars get 15 charms like solars. Jack of trade Dawn buys 3 charms in weapon skills.<br /> A lunar buys 5 strengh charms, 5 dex, etc<br /> I think the lunar would be doing the jack of trades weapon master thing better.<br /> <br /> 2) Doesn't matter if they are jack of all trades. They will still have a few defining skills. The Ninja lunar with dex 5 stealth 5 and thrown 5. will be the best ninja but it means that at least the party can sneak together. The player that focuses on socials will be happy to have other players a long to help. PLaying good cop bad cop for just one example (my mind just came up with 10 ways having 5 shapeshifting social people can rek house).<br /> <br /> Think of it as this. You will have the charater that is best at this or that. But you are not crap at anything. Therefore can support the the person who is best at something instead of just watching<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973135#post973135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose this touches on what I always had most trouble wrapping my head around with lunars. The best way I can put it is in terms of the first age.<br /> The solars part in the first age was being the best. They were the cherry on top of all the amazing stuff. Sure any exalt could fight off a fair folk invasion, but solars could do it better. Sure any exalt could help advance and protect society, but solars could do it best.<br /> The dragon blooded role was basically to fill everything in. Mighty as the celestial exalted are, there are far more problems that require the attention of an exalt then there are exalts around to actually solve them. The DBs change that. Now every single city can have an exalted officer solving crimes, an exalted teacher helping to preserve and pass on knowledge.<br /> The sidereal role was to use foresight to make things run smoother. They are the only ones who can use the loom of fate. They can use it to gather knowledge about the past and future very well, as well as to manipulate events to go how they want them. Their native charms do both those things quite well to. Using those powers they can essentially organize and advise the exalts so that the tasks they have go easier.<br /> In all these cases, losing the exalt type would lessen the first age. .</div> </div> </div> </div>But would it make the 1st age less? Yeah it would because it is writen that why but really. with the way the magic system works now. The solars could of made a supernatraul army as well as summoning demons and elementals to take the dragon blooded role. Smaller gods could taken the role of the Sids looking after fate and adiving. Solars are epic. They would of found a way. Just like the players will do. The first age could still work just the same. The lunars did what the Dragon blooded did. Fight on the front lines, teach mortals and solve crimes a dragon blooded couldnt.. They did what sidereal did. Make things run smoother. Adviced the solars. There are only 100 sids and 300 solars. The sids also where stuck in heaven a lot. Lunars ran nations too. A solar can't be everywhere aswell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=973135#post973135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lose the solars and you lose the best and brightest responsible for the greater parts of the first age. Lose the sidereals and you lose important foresight and have to dedicate more manpower to solving problems as they come up that you would have known about before. Lose the dragon blooded and you lose the hundreds of thousands of men and women who could manage the hundreds of thousands of individual threats across creation.<br /> But what did the lunars do? What role does they play that fell on them alone? Sure they can shapeshifted, but in the grand scheme of things that's simply a means to an end. There didn't appear to me to be anything that lunars could do that the others couldn't. It seemed that if you lost lunars, besides the decrease in raw manpower from losing a bunch of celestial exalts, the first age wouldn't have been really affected.<br /> This thread has been a little helpful though, and I'm interested in seeing where the devs take lunars as the edition unfolds</div> </div> </div> </div>You would lose <b>a lot </b>of man power. In setting Lunars are meant to be able to stand toe-to-toe with solars (even if Lunars are bound to loose). Sids are like mages. Their power comes from planning (and crazy martial arts). They dont have the same raw power as Solars or Lunars. That is why they where the parthers in crime with the solars. Equals that are forever a few steps behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","user":"Mental-State","date":". 09-29-2016, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T04:46:19-07:00","id":978309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=972292#post972292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I still feel like 3E's take on the Lunars was a copout. 'We can't decide what Lunars are so we decided that neither can they! That's their plot arc!' Which doesn't exactly inspire a player, especially compared to the Factions' or the Cult's multiple plot hooks. It sounded to me like Lunars have to be built around the players' group and have no base for an agenda of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are people that have members who still remeber what was taken from them. Seen the great and the bad solars have done. People on the run. Dragons and Sids hunt them down with numbers and fate. Gods want to help but are too scared piss off the realm. The only safe place to hide has no rules and uncountable beings that want to eat your soul. You dont know who to trust but they shouldnt trust you.<br /> <br /> I just had a awesome lunar idea just writing that. I person who doesnt care about exalted politics. Who hates who, what goes on in heaven. He just does what he feel is right. He has the power to do good so he will. I can see him pissed a lot of people off and gaining strange allies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=974325#post974325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People should pick up the Lunar book and go &quot;Wow Lunars are really cool! I want to play a Lunar so I can play a bestial anti-hero who steals the face of a Dragonblood's servant and then sneaks into his room and turns into a giant bear-monster and mauls his face off! That'll be awesome!&quot;<br /> Or, alternatively, &quot;I enjoy problem-solving by having a toolbox of different forms and working out how to leverage them to solve particular problems, rather than just rolling a bucket of dice at them, and Lunar mechanics seem to do this, but in a less wacky way than Sidereal mechanics.&quot;<br /> Or, alternatively, &quot;I want to play a champion of the barbarian peoples who takes the form of their patron animal to lead them to victory.&quot;<br /> Or even &quot;I want to play a werewolf in this fantasy game. Werewolves are cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because if they pick up the book and go &quot;So, the point of these guys is the gods made them to kind of do a bit of everything because the other Exalts were more specialised?&quot; Well, that's not very inspiring. It's probably going to make you want to play one of these other more interesting-sounding splats</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally love the idea playing a guy that <b>can </b>fall back on being a jack of all trades. But focus on a certain role. That can be a bard for 20 years then just swicth to a painter one day and do ok from it from day one. Instead of spending years now mastering a new craft.<br /> <br /> But I see your point. I dont think the lunars should be sold to people saying they are the bit of everything splat. I do think it is a problem from 2nd ed where everything has a place and everything was statted. Everything needed a role. Solars where not god kings at first. All exalted where soliders. They where not made to rule the world. I think people forget that. They was given that role after they was made. The Sids where the only ones that have the same role they always did. Dragonblooded took their morden role.<br /> <br /> Getting back to lunars. Change jack of all trade to adaptable. The one exalt that can expect to survive anything. Yes in a solar <i>can </i>but they have to build that way. Spend xp. A lunar just from their excellenies and shapeshifting without charms are the most likely to surive alien worlds. New diseases and poisons. Going without air.<br /> They should (I believe) be the best exalt crafting artifacts in the middle of nowhere with the most wood and stone bound for tools.<br /> Fuck finesse, enough raw power will solve anything.<br /> <br /> The two biggest themes for the Lunars is<br /> To survive and adapt. I know lunars have had a hard time but they themes are there somewhere in the first and second book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","user":"Mental-State","date":". 09-29-2016, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:46:51-07:00","id":978513,"title":"","content":"One of my potentially out-there theories for the Lunar foil is going to be an inversion of their tinfoil hat theories of MoEP: Lunars where the Solars are portrayed as actively and maliciously trying to keep them down. What if the Lunars of the distant past not only embraced the role as second to the Solars (assuming the five caste structure in the process) but pushed someone else out to get there?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:56:19-07:00","id":978519,"title":"","content":"That sounds awesome but I wouldn't make it canon. Make it a maybe in the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:44:46-07:00","id":978679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-State</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=978302#post978302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) A Full moon meele lunar in a fight could add most of his charms to a bow or his fist/claws/etc. Lets say lunars get 15 charms like solars. Jack of trade Dawn buys 3 charms in weapon skills.<br /> A lunar buys 5 strengh charms, 5 dex, etc<br /> I think the lunar would be doing the jack of trades weapon master thing better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be so, esp. Solars have those supernal abilities that encourage them to be specialists, but it feels not that intuitive that if a player were to go <br /> <br /> &quot;My Solar Dawn's concept is to be a well rounded, universal master of weapons and fighting&quot;<br /> <br /> then the Lunar is automatically doing that better. (And that's not usually the kind of thing I would concern about with Solar Exalted.).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:09:02-07:00","id":978808,"title":"","content":"The Lunars role in Creation is actually very simple and I thought pretty well defined in the First Edition which got swept aside in all of the noise. The Lunars role is to survive, look at who Luna chooses: The slave who seeks to escape, there is an easy way to escape-kill yourself, Luna does not choose that person. Instead she chooses the slave that uses his/her looks or charm as currency and then while the Master lays sleeping pulls the tent stake and uses a hammer to nail him/her to the ground. Luna chooses the ship-wrecked survivor that uses his wits to escape from the visiting pirates while rigging traps to defend his new home. Luna's choosen are the ultimate in adapt and survive, the Wyld Hunt has tracked you to a small valley, but you have taken the heart-blood of the elderly hermit that rarely visits town but whom everyone will vouch was born there. The Death Knight has driven you to the edge of a cliff, you shift into a bird and flee. <br /> I may very well be wrong and I firmly expect to hear how wrong I am, but this is my take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:44:16-07:00","id":978871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=978808#post978808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars role in Creation is actually very simple and I thought pretty well defined in the First Edition which got swept aside in all of the noise. The Lunars role is to survive, look at who Luna chooses: The slave who seeks to escape, there is an easy way to escape-kill yourself, Luna does not choose that person. Instead she chooses the slave that uses his/her looks or charm as currency and then while the Master lays sleeping pulls the tent stake and uses a hammer to nail him/her to the ground. Luna chooses the ship-wrecked survivor that uses his wits to escape from the visiting pirates while rigging traps to defend his new home. Luna's choosen are the ultimate in adapt and survive,<b> the Wyld Hunt has tracked you to a small valley, but you have taken the heart-blood of the elderly hermit that rarely visits town but whom everyone will vouch was born there.</b> The Death Knight has driven you to the edge of a cliff, you shift into a bird and flee.<br /> I may very well be wrong and I firmly expect to hear how wrong I am, but this is my take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for adaptability and flexibility, but not so keen on the portrayal of Lunars as cowards who callously throw away human lives - individually, for their Heart's Blood, or by the hundreds or thousands as expendable shock-troops - all so that they can survive one more precious day. I prefer that moral conflict arise organically from difficult and <i>relatable </i>situations within the context of the gameworld, irrespective of splat, instead of pigeonholing one group as &quot;The Bad-Guy Splat&quot; by giving them Skill Focus: Being A Bastard. Sociopathic parasitism isn't necessarily out of genre for Exalted in general and Lunars in particular, but I'd rather it be something they <i>do </i>rather than something they <i>are</i>. The World of Darkness, this ain't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T00:35:13-07:00","id":978901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=978679#post978679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be so, esp. Solars have those supernal abilities that encourage them to be specialists, but it feels not that intuitive that if a player were to go<br /> <br /> &quot;My Solar Dawn's concept is to be a well rounded, universal master of weapons and fighting&quot;<br /> <br /> then the Lunar is automatically doing that better. (And that's not usually the kind of thing I would concern about with Solar Exalted.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Lunars have to be good at something. Sids are the best with fate <i>and </i>SMAs.<br /> Just having Lunar having just shapeshifting as the only thing they have over Solars is a bit lame. A Solar around enough can <b>master </b>every skill and beat the lunar at it everytime. A Solar will at some point with all the exp in the world be better so let the Lunar have there time in the sun (LOOL). Because it will not last long. Certain splats lends itself to different play styles, therefrore certain modes of play will work better with certain ones. If you want to play a spy then you will be the best one to choose in Vampire the Requim is a Meket, doesn't mean you can't do as a Deva.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about ex 3rd is that the lines are blured with different exalts when it comes to power. Dragon Blooded (by what the devs said and want to do) are not the exalted mooks.<br /> Yes a Solar in a white room will always win. The setting is written that way but the setting is also written that the solar all lost in the first age. How was they beaten though? Well do not play Solars at their own game. The best people to do it is the Lunars.<br /> Imagine if the Lunars helped take down the Solars and worked with the dragon blooded. I don't think the Solars would have a chance to come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:22:23-07:00","id":978946,"title":"","content":"I think a reinvigoration of the Wyld especially with some more enaging plot hooks would greatly help flesh out Lunars. Also adding more depth to Fair Folk protagonists would help. I think having the Wyld as a formless incoherent and mutable mass populated only by creatures that are Bent on the destruction of form to be a not very good playing space. If there were battlefields that Lunars were warring against the fair folk in the border marches what would it look like? What about a dominion that is populated by Raksha but they pay homage to a Lunar mistress, An exotic Wyld market Freehold ever moving and steeped in politics but by no means hostile to creation or its denizens. Lunars fighting alongside Fair Folk Nobles to repel Hannya or a nearby necrotising Shadow Land.<br /> <br /> To be honest I always felt Wyld Shaping and Wyld Shaping Technique should be Lunars Purview. BUt as it isnt Wyld Questing could be something compelling for Lunars. To increase resources like Artifacts or allies but also as a way to shed Limit, or learn new forms. I think it adds to their story that the force they are fighting against the Realm is also the force the are ring feincing and protecting from the Wyld. At the same time they have a huge amount of empathy for Raksha as they are also quixotic mutable beings that are having another groups Hegemony pushed on them.<br /> <br /> So yeah Shapeshifting is their thing and I think their place (like the Sids is Yu Shan) should be the Wyld which needs to be more compelling and engaging. This will inform what Lunar Stories can look like more than just guerilla warfare against the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:47:10-07:00","id":979068,"title":"","content":"I agree very much so. I just feel that the guerilla warefare with the realm was needed too. Sids have things to do in heaven and creation. Should be the same thing for Lunars which is more than find solar mate/revenge on solar mate.<br /> What I want to see mechanicly is an Luna exalt cappable of having a war with Dragons, Sids and the Wyld and is still going strong. They are the enermy of mostly everything and that for me is a good reason they havent won <b><i>yet </i></b>but they could.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:01:28-07:00","id":979440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=978946#post978946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a reinvigoration of the Wyld especially with some more enaging plot hooks would greatly help flesh out Lunars. Also adding more depth to Fair Folk protagonists would help. I think having the Wyld as a formless incoherent and mutable mass populated only by creatures that are Bent on the destruction of form to be a not very good playing space. If there were battlefields that Lunars were warring against the fair folk in the border marches what would it look like? What about a dominion that is populated by Raksha but they pay homage to a Lunar mistress, An exotic Wyld market Freehold ever moving and steeped in politics but by no means hostile to creation or its denizens. Lunars fighting alongside Fair Folk Nobles to repel Hannya or a nearby necrotising Shadow Land.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems very close to second edition, which is what we're almost certainly not getting again. Particularly because Lunars aren't tied to the Wyld at all from what we've seen; they're still in Creation, fighting in Creation for control over Creation, bit by bit. The Wyld is days, weeks, or months of travel away, and the denizens that they encounter are strange and unusual to them, too. Any such freehold is going to be a one-off, not a constant wherever Lunars and Fair Folk find their influence spilling over. Not the least reason for which being that there isn't an infinite supply of Fair Folk anymore, just waiting to boil over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be honest I always felt Wyld Shaping and Wyld Shaping Technique should be Lunars Purview. BUt as it isnt Wyld Questing could be something compelling for Lunars. To increase resources like Artifacts or allies but also as a way to shed Limit, or learn new forms. I think it adds to their story that the force they are fighting against the Realm is also the force the are ring feincing and protecting from the Wyld. At the same time they have a huge amount of empathy for Raksha as they are also quixotic mutable beings that are having another groups Hegemony pushed on them.<br /> <br /> So yeah Shapeshifting is their thing and I think their place (like the Sids is Yu Shan) should be the Wyld which needs to be more compelling and engaging. This will inform what Lunar Stories can look like more than just guerilla warfare against the realm. </div> </div> </div>There is no equivalent to Yu Shan for Lunars, because the Lunar struggle against the Sidereals is not symmetrical. The Sidereals get their cool kids clubhouse in heaven because they took actions to secure their position in it, not because it's a law of the universe to hand out cool kids clubhouses to every major faction.The Lunars don't have one because they got chased out of their original home on pain of death a long time ago, and took to the wilderness to hide and strike back. Sidereals are blocking heaven, and the Dragon-Blooded are blocking the Blessed Isle. That's why the Lunars ended up reshaped into a more monstrous likeness, ready to do battle without any support structure to speak of and then fade away. It's not an existence that makes them more sympathetic to Fair Folk, I'd imagine, since most of the time they're going to encounter Fair Folk in a lot of the same contexts as Solars, i.e. they're attacking people that the Lunar cares about and now it's time for some largely justifiable ultraviolence to stop the attacks and rescue captives. As the elites of their culture, raksha, the nobles, are also likely to come across as being just as abrasive and callous as Dynasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T23:03:16-07:00","id":979526,"title":"","content":"None of the Exalted have roles.<br /> <br /> Many of them, however, have responsibilities. That the Sidereals alone shared a common one is why they won.<br /> <br /> &lt;/hot_take&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:59:51-07:00","id":979630,"title":"","content":"Mmm. There's a few things I <u>want</u> Lunars to be capable of.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Warning: Many analogies ahead, and I have no idea what anyone is planning for Lunar 3E</span><br /> <br /> First off, survival like some folks mentioned. Solars <u>tame </u>the Wyld, lock it down and turn it into whatever part of Creation they need. Lunars <u>use/inhabit</u> the Wyld by adapting to it. Which definitely means they need to be able to resist the mental effects as easily as the physical. Another part of that is Lunars shouldn't need infrastructure. Solars lead and get groups together to do big things, where a Lunar would do it themselves or do without. (Solar crafter in the wilderness: use 'need no tools' type charms to build better and better tools, and eventually make/acquire minions to handle the non-crafting stuff. A Lunar goes nekkid and uses claws, or makes a flint axe and uses Lunar charms to make it a great weapon for that Lunar.)<br /> <br /> Second would be infiltration. A Solar would use a disguise, or might go as far as a Cylon (brainwash self to think you are the role). A Lunar routinely does a Kimball Kinnison - replace some minion on the inside, then the minion 'suddenly' shows 'more potential' and quickly goes up the ranks. Solar would be better at a short con, the Lunar does the lifelong mole thing. Especially if, say, you want to infiltrate someone's Blood Ape army. Also, a Solar taking over a town is all 'glorious skilled human who you want to follow'. The Lunar way would be 'I'm a new, strange looking god or elemental spirit. Worship me and accept some taboos.&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as the Solar thing, that type of Lunar would be a balance for a <u>specific</u> Solar. In D&amp;D, one of them is the backstabbing rogue, the other is the fighter who flanks to let the rogue do his thing. Lunars would be big on synergy. That also means that a all-Lunar group tries to synergize with each other. (and there are some things a Solar just can't do well because they only have one body. Having that second pair of hands can help)<br /> <br /> Assuming Lunars are still attribute-based, and the Ex3 take on excellencies, I would guess that Lunars start with all 9. To me that means better than mortal level at everything, but still needs charms to do non-mortal or much much better than mortal stuff. Any Lunar can code a 3D shooter, but it takes a specialist to make the graphics engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:54:46-07:00","id":979658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=979440#post979440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no equivalent to Yu Shan for Lunars, because the Lunar struggle against the Sidereals is not symmetrical. The Sidereals get their cool kids clubhouse in heaven because they took actions to secure their position in it, not because it's a law of the universe to hand out cool kids clubhouses to every major faction.The Lunars don't have one because they got chased out of their original home on pain of death a long time ago, and took to the wilderness to hide and strike back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yu-Shan is as much of a weakness as any medieval castle was when facing the steppe hordes. It shouldn't be looked upon as an advantage. It should be seen as an albatross.<br /> <br /> Let me discuss the problems with the geopolitical perspective of 1e/2e and how they relate to the Lunar Exalted. Owing to the influence of work like 'Conan', the barbarian cliche of 2e was very western, very European in character. It proposed primitives that were attacking in 'screaming hordes' only to be cut down by the Realm Legions, rarely gaining ground except when given aid by a Lunar Anathema. It proposed such attacks as a nuisance, kept at bay by the ever-expanding 'Roman/Chinese' Realm.<br /> <br /> This is utterly unlike history tells us the 'barbarian hordes' that ACTUALLY ravaged the world were.<br /> <br /> The reality of the 'barbarian cliche' is that these were not primitive people. In fact, they were (by far) the most sophisticated military tacticians of the era, who understood not only the conventional siege-based warfare of the west but also the value of mobility and the critical nature of supply. The Exalted cliche is a horde attacking with immense numbers and being turned back by the noble shields of civilized society. The reality, far different, has groups of 'barbarians' defeated forces with more than 10 times their number.<br /> <br /> That's right. With a 10-1 advantage, with siege fortification in place, with extensive military traditions going back centuries... China AND European forces, including some of the most well provisioned and prepared in that era, were defeated. Over and over. And not just defeated - absolutely crushed.<br /> <br /> Exalted borrows from the European 'barbarian cliche' even more when it suggests a society based upon rubbing twigs together and shamanic magic. In truth, the actual barbarian hordes that people like Ma-Ha-Suchi are based on were ruthless about absorbing, maintaining and USING the technology of every culture they came into contact with. Contrary to the expectation of many modern readers, the barbarians showed up with SUPERIOR siege technology and SUPERIOR siege engineers.<br /> <br /> Exalted has always had a major issue with pushing barbarians into the cliche box, and never was this more profoundly demonstrated than with Lunar Exalted. They should be portrayed as a force engaged in 'Neo-Warfare', just like the steppe barbarians were, with none of the condescension or implied cultural superiority that Exalted has discussed these people with over the last decade.<br /> <br /> To the people who understood what 'barbarians' were in the real world in the context of actually living in the period, they were... the end of the world. An unstoppable force. And this happened MULTIPLE times in history. In fact, much of Chinese military policy and political theory was based upon the idea of preventing it from ever happening again, because they knew once these people started fighting?... they were not only 'to be respected', but they were essentially invincible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:11:14-07:00","id":979664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=979658#post979658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yu-Shan is as much of a weakness as any medieval castle was when facing the steppe hordes. It shouldn't be looked upon as an advantage. It should be seen as an albatross.<br /> <br /> Let me discuss the problems with the geopolitical perspective of 1e/2e and how they relate to the Lunar Exalted. Owing to the influence of work like 'Conan', the barbarian cliche of 2e was very western, very European in character. It proposed primitives that were attacking in 'screaming hordes' only to be cut down by the Realm Legions, rarely gaining ground except when given aid by a Lunar Anathema. It proposed such attacks as a nuisance, kept at bay by the ever-expanding 'Roman/Chinese' Realm.<br /> <br /> This is utterly unlike history tells us the 'barbarian hordes' that ACTUALLY ravaged the world were.<br /> <br /> The reality of the 'barbarian cliche' is that these were not primitive people. In fact, they were (by far) the most sophisticated military tacticians of the era, who understood not only the conventional siege-based warfare of the west but also the value of mobility and the critical nature of supply. The Exalted cliche is a horde attacking with immense numbers and being turned back by the noble shields of civilized society. The reality, far different, has groups of 'barbarians' defeated forces with more than 10 times their number.<br /> <br /> That's right. With a 10-1 advantage, with siege fortification in place, with extensive military traditions going back centuries... China AND European forces, including some of the most well provisioned and prepared in that era, were defeated. Over and over. And not just defeated - absolutely crushed.</div> </div> </div> </div>And middle-eastern forces, too. I've read a biography of Genghis Khan, I know how it worked out in history. (He'd actually be an Eclipse Solar!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted borrows from the European 'barbarian cliche' even more when it suggests a society based upon rubbing twigs together and shamanic magic. In truth, the actual barbarian hordes that people like Ma-Ha-Suchi are based on were ruthless about absorbing, maintaining and USING the technology of every culture they came into contact with. Contrary to the expectation of many modern readers, the barbarians showed up with SUPERIOR siege technology and SUPERIOR siege engineers.<br /> <br /> Exalted has always had a major issue with pushing barbarians into the cliche box, and never was this more profoundly demonstrated than with Lunar Exalted. They should be portrayed as a force engaged in 'Neo-Warfare', just like the steppe barbarians were, with none of the condescension or implied cultural superiority that Exalted has discussed these people with over the last decade. </div> </div> </div>The problem here being that Exalted isn't a game of inventing past the enemy on historical earth. It doesn't have a system set up for general technological advancement, because it isn't happening in a fantasy Mad Max world. It happened millennia ago, and the wrecked remains of it are what everyone has to work with. So if they get their hands on, say, a warstrider, it's going to get used, but it needs to be used so that the Dragon-Blooded exhaust more than one warstrider to take it down. And they will take it down, because they have more of the stockpiled ancient sorcery, but the stockpiles can't hold out forever. And if the Dragon-Blooded can be made to blow their wad on stuff that wouldn't normally require it, so much the better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To the people who understood what 'barbarians' were in the real world in the context of actually living in the period, they were... the end of the world. An unstoppable force. And this happened MULTIPLE times in history. In fact, much of Chinese military policy and political theory was based upon the idea of preventing it from ever happening again, because they knew once these people started fighting?... they were not only 'to be respected', but they were essentially invincible. </div> </div> </div>How much of that is based on having people who can pull off Dynasty Warriors levels of personally-inflicted carnage at the drop of a hat? Because they exist on both sides, but the Dragon-Blooded have way more of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:30:49-07:00","id":979679,"title":"","content":"The larger point I'm trying to make is about the bias. It begins at screaming hordes and ends at firm ideas about 'thematics' which suggest Lunar Exalted shouldn't craft very much, and CERTAINLY shouldn't use TOOLS to do so, so they like... beat swords out of rocks or sing arrows out of moonsilver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:12:14-07:00","id":979706,"title":"","content":"I think they become screaming hordes as they are just mortals fighting the realm which is exalted. Dragon blood will have the best tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:23:47-07:00","id":979745,"title":"","content":"The Chinese started off with better technology, as well. The 'barbarians' were clever enough to impress Chinese savants into service. Now as written, Exalted barbarians would probably decry such methods as 'tools of the enemy' or something equally silly and go back to dancing around bonfires half-naked. By contrast, real world examples of militarized 'barbarian' cultures were much more pragmatic and eager to adopt the tools of other military traditions, just so long as they worked.<br /> <br /> This leads directly into another one of the more ridiculous precepts of the settings, the idea that 'only the realm' uses Dragonblooded officers and that somehow, the Realm has managed to horde the genetic legacy of the Terrestrial Exalted. Hostages and prisoners do not exist in this setting, despite the fact that they play a very real role in military history in any real world situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:29:20-07:00","id":979747,"title":"","content":"To be fair, actually the Bull of the North's barbarian army used Dragonblood lieutenants, and the Haslanti, a country of Barbarians forged into a nation by a Lunar, are Inuit-types wielding crossbows and using hot air balloons, hangliders, and even zeppelins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mental-State, Lunars are cunning, I doubt they actually go in for commanding screaming hordes.<br /> <br /> Jungle warriors who draw the Realm into the dense trees where they can shoot them with their poisoned blowgun needles, yes. Horse archers who draw the heavy realm infantry across the steppe, dropping the Realm's finest from a distance while staying always out of range, sure. Northern raiders whose longships crash onto the shores of a Satrapy, murder the Monks, and then vanish back into the trackless ocean, absolutely. Savage wolfmen who ambush Realm columns with their Elkmen-blessed weaponry, sharkmen who grap a Realm ship in the middle of the ocean, forest-tribes equipped in lightweight-yet-impenetrable ironwood armour, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> But a horde of men in furs with badly-made axes who run screaming straight into a disciplined Realm phalanx? Unless this is a plan to distract the Realm, or cull their internal rivals, or something like that, is not something many Lunars are stupid enough to order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-01-2016, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:55:08-07:00","id":979756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=979679#post979679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The larger point I'm trying to make is about the bias. It begins at screaming hordes and ends at firm ideas about 'thematics' which suggest Lunar Exalted shouldn't craft very much, and CERTAINLY shouldn't use TOOLS to do so, so they like... beat swords out of rocks or sing arrows out of moonsilver.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">what we've been told</a> on the matter. Besides, the point remains that we're not dealing with a perfectly historical context here. Far from it, it's like magical Mad Max after nearly a millennium and a half of backsliding. All the cars and bullets are getting rarer, it's hard to find gas to fuel said cars, and there's one or two places that are hoarding the most of them and using them pretty much just to try and kill the other side.<br /> <br /> (Lookshy, assuming that you can stay away from its Wyld Hunts, sort of makes the Lunars' task easier in this regard, and some of them might be trying to provoke the Realm to try and send in special assets so that they can see both sides wear each other down without any effort on their part).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:59:28-07:00","id":979836,"title":"","content":"@ Piff, mostly close to things I would agree with, and a good post to make, though as a grace note, I guess would personally articulate this a little differently, as I feel like this is a bit more hype that could overestimate the &quot;barbarians&quot;* or that people could dismiss though. <br /> <br /> I would point out the barbarian peoples who made big splashes tended not to be 10-1 in actual soldiers (though I don't think you're implying they were), because of quite high mobilisation of men, and tended to have more in the cavalry in particular, and at the same time people from the steppe basically tended to have an interest in conquering China that wasn't as much in the reverse direction (because people on the steppe basically had nothing by the standards of wealth). Then they seized upon the opportunity to invade mainly China (but also the Middle East and South Asia), when internal factionalisation provided it and when the people in the settled world were also weak at funding and supporting the military and at using their technology and resources to its maximum.<br /> <br /> (In our history the advantages of the steppe cultures being able to mobilise high %s and the technological advantages of lots of cavalry tended to drop pretty fast by the time you had guys like the (mostly sedentary and &quot;civilized&quot;) Manchu and Russians and the Gunpowder Empires on the scene, and then certainly with later Western European colonialisation. But there was a time between the fall of Rome and the rise of Gunpowder Empires and early modern empires who could leverage their economies' superior wealth and infrastructure, when the technology was right for cultures from the steppe to be in zenith as conquerors and imperialists, even with no real settled base of wealth and power).<br /> <br /> I point this because, though we would say it differently, you can have the Lunars being leaders of barbarian forces who have really great mobilisation of their cultures and they have pretty good gear and cooperate well and the Realm doesn't really want to take a fight to them because they're losing money every time they do, and they're great at picking when and where the Realm is internally divided. Then with all these factors so they've got a good chance. And I think a lot of the older stuff did say this, but just said it in kind of a lame way that was easy to dismiss as hyping up &quot;dumb&quot; strategies (basically undercut the ideas the Lunars could be effective with a kind of &quot;They have no strategy and no gear and specifically field fewer warriors in battles and also have a huge cultural arrogance&quot; vibe). (Though I don't know if Creation really has the right geography for anything like the importance for the specific steppe barbarians from our history.)<br /> <br /> * I haven't scare-quoted &quot;barbarians&quot; for the rest of the post because it's pretty boring to do and read, but assume I have if you'd like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T00:33:47-07:00","id":980143,"title":"","content":"I think it does have the right geography, considering that the north, scavenger lands and south have a lot of open space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T03:20:18-07:00","id":980183,"title":"","content":"Yes, possibly. Though for the same situation with pastoralist groups, it's more if it's open grassland good to raise horses and cattle and ruminants though, not so much open space which is good for cereal agriculture, or desert or tundra. (Just looking over the 2e map, the groups I think of as the horse people, Marukan and Delzahn, seem to be sitting on top of mountain ranges?). Maybe there should be more and more significant groups like that around. <br /> <br /> The Scavenger Lands always looks on a map like it has the most China like geography (lots of plains, big rivers running on the east-west axis, not north-south), so I guess if you could have a similar situation there, but without the political and cultural unity of China.<br /> <br /> (I think it's interesting to think about how the geography is different, and wouldn't recapitulate much of the geography of Eurasia, so you wouldn't get the same kind of dynamics, exactly.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:24:25-07:00","id":980253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=979747#post979747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mental-State, Lunars are cunning</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more the realms thoughts on them and also the fact that any mortal army would look like untrained horde compared to exalted trained army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:58:53-07:00","id":980313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=980183#post980183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, possibly. Though for the same situation with pastoralist groups, it's more if it's open grassland good to raise horses and cattle and ruminants though, not so much open space which is good for cereal agriculture, or desert or tundra. (Just looking over the 2e map, the groups I think of as the horse people, Marukan and Delzahn, seem to be sitting on top of mountain ranges?). Maybe there should be more and more significant groups like that around.<br /> <br /> The Scavenger Lands always looks on a map like it has the most China like geography (lots of plains, big rivers running on the east-west axis, not north-south), so I guess if you could have a similar situation there, but without the political and cultural unity of China.<br /> <br /> (I think it's interesting to think about how the geography is different, and wouldn't recapitulate much of the geography of Eurasia, so you wouldn't get the same kind of dynamics, exactly.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Delzahn started next to the mountains, then, being a horse-riding horde, migrated north-west across the desert to conquer the settled peoples on the coast.<br /> <br /> The Scavenger Lands does say that, historically, it has been invaded a few times by barbarian armies like the Arzhecki, though those aren't horse-riders. But also Medo, who I think are, and are at the top of the Scavenger Lands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:47:45-07:00","id":980334,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Medo are described as formerly cavalry based raiders with cavalry, clan based, and they currently serve the Realm as janissaries. Overlaps with steppe groups. Their signature cultural achievement is walling off the mountain passes to their north (against what? shadowlands? pretty intriguing hook), they're hill tribes and they've a capital city. Sort of like the steppe groups to China and sort of not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:23:45-07:00","id":980377,"title":"","content":"They also used to have a big empire, until the Realm beat them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T22:18:00-07:00","id":980585,"title":"","content":"I have only played 3E exalted and do not carry any knowledge of the previous editions or of W:tA either although I know what it is. Just from the 3E book I get the impression the Lunars honestly have several big clues into who/what they are/do. I think they currently are the main reason the Wyld is not lapping at the shores of the blessed isle right now. I just get the impression they are battling the fae back making kingdoms in the Middlemarches to keep them from going full Wyld. In this respect I think their shape changing powers are most likely the best defense against being horribly warped or consumed by the Wyld.<br /> <br /> In addition to this it seems like they have a complex relationship with the Solars. Like they used to be favored consorts/lovers/confidants as well as in some cases treated as slaves and fodder like Dragon Blooded. I am just guessing but I think the disconnect between Lunars and Solars most likely starting occurring due to depredations Solars did during limit breaks in which they were lashed out at or their hearts were broken watching their loved one or admired one literally turn into a monster.<br /> <br /> The information in the 3E core book seems to imply the Lunars were the most trusted confidants of the Solars and often acted on behalf or for them. Although I do not personally know anything about Gaia/Luna just from reading the forums I have picked up some understanding of them. I think Lunars stepped into the the role of Guarding creation as well as a strong desire to destroy those who slew the Solars and ruined the world with their actions and selfishness. Honestly it seems like the Lunars got the Anathema tag due to loyalty or love not due to them being monstrous destroyers or kings of excess. The book seems to imply the Lunars as a whole fared a lot better then the Solars did in surviving purges overall. Which means there are probably still grieving lovers, bitter idealists, vengeance seeking friends out there that remember and possibly personally know or even commanded the leaders of the houses. Knowing the faces and personalities of the traitors who destroyed so much of the world has to be a potent reason for revenge and hate. <br /> <br /> So to stop meandering I think Lunars will be the balances and defenders. The explorers and sages. I think their role in creation was and will be the ones who explored the edges of the world, keep and kept it safe, and tempered the Solars in their excesses to keep them from becoming the monsters they could devolve into when they limit break. I am willing to bet limit breaks would have been much much more common without Lunars. I think the role of defender became much more prominent after the Solars fell.<br /> <br /> Anyway as an ignorant of previous settings gamer that was my impression of my read through of the 3E core book in relation to Lunars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:17:03-07:00","id":980649,"title":"","content":"I think Lunars have to be in someway inextricably linked to the Wyld. Their Patron has strong links to it. And not just as someone who battles it but someone who courts it and flirts with it. Sometime's she is at the UCS side fighting it back and sometimes he is frollicking in the oceans of madness and I think Lunars should have this side to them.<br /> <br /> Dont get me wrong their will be many lunars in the outer threshold but still close to the Blessed Isle fixated on what they lost and getting revenge on their usurpers, standing against tyranny and fighting a global super power, or just protecting their patch of Creation from outside aggressors. But lets remember the Lunars were comfortable in the Wyld before the Usurpation. They chose it as their refuge during the usurpation and they have helped protect Creation's borders from it. For me this gives them a very strong and not always antagonistic relationship with it. <br /> <br /> Even a Blessed Isle/Inner Threshold centric Lunar could be able to Wyld Quest for their development arc and it gives them something unique and in keeping thematically. for their Splat. The Full moon who battles in the Cataphractoi in the Wyld for a new weapon or to achieve a permanent physical mutation by surviving and addictive and toxic landscape that seeks his corruption, the No moon who spirit quests to induct themselves into a sorcerous path or who crafts a minor fay into a familiar or bind it in a moon-like orb that floats around the Lunar, A changing moon who is the only Creation bound creature capable of playing in the intricate and illogical webs of the great Raksha Courts, who is bestowed a powerful love token from his otherworldly paramour or tricks an Unshaped who takes the form of a giant Goblin market and vexes it for a boon it can take back to creation.<br /> <br /> I don' think this breaks their new interpretation as the bestial, barbaric other on the fringes of society rageing against the Scarlet Empire. I think it compliments this feel. The questing warrior, the spirit shaman and the primal trickster are all very much tropes of the barbarian, primitive, animalistic culture they are trying to evoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:06:07-07:00","id":980775,"title":"","content":"Ya know, Zeus was a Lunar, and maybe Odin (forget if he was a shapeshifter or if his disguise was just &quot;gandalf with eye patch&quot;). Hopefully the charms will be there to use them as inspiration for less-barbarian-y characters.<br /> <br /> Actually, a Lunar circle being a region's pantheon might be the start of a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:27:11-07:00","id":980869,"title":"","content":"I really love the two attribute aspect of the new Lunar Excellency.<br /> The developers had been saying that they wanted the Lunars to be physical which had made me somewhat worried but when I saw that it instantly clicked with me. It could have been Hulk Smash but instead I now envision social Lunars using a lot of body language while more intellectual ones new blend sensory input with recently acquired knowledge, this is so much better for them than Relentless Lunar Fury and its equivalents were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:43:45-07:00","id":981131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=980649#post980649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lunars have to be in someway inextricably linked to the Wyld. Their Patron has strong links to it. And not just as someone who battles it but someone who courts it and flirts with it. Sometime's she is at the UCS side fighting it back and sometimes he is frollicking in the oceans of madness and I think Lunars should have this side to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this had its time, and that it seems to be something that's on its way out, if not gone already. Having strong ties to the Wyld tends to detract from the role of the Fair Folk, too, so it helps two splats if the Lunars have nothing to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:53:23-07:00","id":981177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981131#post981131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that this had its time, and that it seems to be something that's on its way out, if not gone already. Having strong ties to the Wyld tends to detract from the role of the Fair Folk, too, so it helps two splats if the Lunars have nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even so, after having spent so much time there, I'd hope the Lunars would have come away with SOMETHING other than Chimerism and &quot;I Went To The Wyld And All I Got Were These Stupid Tattoos&quot;. A splat doesn't have to be inextricably linked to the Wyld to have charms that specifically interact with it - does Wyld-Shaping Technique make <i>Solars </i>the &quot;Wyld Exalted&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T20:05:58-07:00","id":981229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981177#post981177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even so, after having spent so much time there, I'd hope the Lunars would have come away with SOMETHING other than Chimerism and &quot;I Went To The Wyld And All I Got Were These Stupid Tattoos&quot;. A splat doesn't have to be inextricably linked to the Wyld to have charms that specifically interact with it - does Wyld-Shaping Technique make <i>Solars </i>the &quot;Wyld Exalted&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimerism has nothing to do with the Wyld now. Finally. And no one argued that Solars were Wyld Exalted, so please don't set that strawman up. We're talking about the old stuff that Lunars were saddled with, like the &quot;benefit&quot; of being able to learn an over-done and confusing system of Charms or having a bunch of really cool effects that they couldn't use in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T01:21:54-07:00","id":981338,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm just a bit a cynical of there being a type of Exalted who's patron has strong links to the Wyld, who have a history of both battling the Wyld and using it as a refuge, who represent themes of animalism, shape changing and &quot;barbarian&quot; culture (where Wyld Barbarian, Wyld beasts and Wyld mutations are all strongly linked to these themes), who have moonsilver tattoos specifically to help them both mutate in creation and hold form in the wyld, now have nothing whatsoever to do with the Wyld. It seems to take lots away without adding anything to me. While it is true Raksha are creatures of the Wyld I dont see them treading on each others conceptual space. Liminals don't tread on Abyssals space yet interacting at the edges of the Underworld as Lunars do with the Wyld works. The Lunar's have close links to the Wyld than any other Exalt type (raskha are not exalts) I fail to see what is gained by rewarding this. I get that the benefits of being able to participate in Shaping combat was pretty limited and difficult to use. So re-imagining how the Wyld informs their aesthetic and mechanics is key but I think severing that tie is out of context for them and takes away an interesting arena for story and development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:01:14-07:00","id":981390,"title":"","content":"As a big fan of Lunars, here's my take on it. Grain of salt. Rule Zero. My own interpretation, etc etc etc.<br /> <br /> Having Lunars (or any other Celestial level Exalted) as second-fiddle Ed McMahons to the Solar level Exalted is terrible writing. It limits our options players and storytellers can engage with, unless we do a lot of finagling to work around the limitations. Some parts of earlier editions really seemed like Lunars and Sidereals (and probably Alchemicals - I never quite caught up with them, nor with Raksha) should just be grateful to sit at the kid's table while the grownups were talking. <br /> <br /> I would like to see a well-played, in-theme Lunar be right on par with an equally well-played, in-theme Solar. I mean that in a storytelling sense more than in a dice crunch sense, because that's how I emphasize my games. A Lunar who's using the right Shape, Transformation, Fury, etc for the situation should be an iconic terror. That, of course, applies for Solars using their perfected skills well, for Sidereals twisting Destiny their way, and so on across the board. Emphasizing theme should be rewarded with crunch.<br /> <br /> The theme that I'd like to see for Lunars is that they change themselves in order to change the world. <br /> <br /> As a short aside here, and so you know where I'm coming from, I'd also like to see Terrestrials brought closer to level in power and coolness. Their specific theme being amazing teamwork, a pair of them should be about on par with a young Celestial, a Circle of them about on par with a pre-centennial Celestial, and beyond that notions of parity get strained anyway.<br /> <br /> I prefer the idea that each of the Celestines &amp; Primordials brought their own nature to their Exalted, but not roles or responsibilities per se. It seems very out of character to me that those sorts of beings would be at all concerned with the details of their creations' tactics and decisions. Rather: &quot;You exist as I have made you. That is enough.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:35:48-07:00","id":981463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981338#post981338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm just a bit a cynical of there being a type of Exalted who's patron has strong links to the Wyld, who have a history of both battling the Wyld and using it as a refuge, who represent themes of animalism, shape changing and &quot;barbarian&quot; culture (where Wyld Barbarian, Wyld beasts and Wyld mutations are all strongly linked to these themes), who have moonsilver tattoos specifically to help them both mutate in creation and hold form in the wyld, now have nothing whatsoever to do with the Wyld. It seems to take lots away without adding anything to me. While it is true Raksha are creatures of the Wyld I dont see them treading on each others conceptual space. Liminals don't tread on Abyssals space yet interacting at the edges of the Underworld as Lunars do with the Wyld works. The Lunar's have close links to the Wyld than any other Exalt type (raskha are not exalts) I fail to see what is gained by rewarding this. I get that the benefits of being able to participate in Shaping combat was pretty limited and difficult to use. So re-imagining how the Wyld informs their aesthetic and mechanics is key but I think severing that tie is out of context for them and takes away an interesting arena for story and development.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be overplaying the link of Luna to the Wyld. Especially since EX3 seems to be emphasizing her connection to Gaia more, particularly on the front of her Exalted. Her entry in the lexicon certainly doesn't mention the Wyld, nor does her description in the list of the Incarna. The only relation we're given is that Lunars fight Fair Folk along with the forces of the Realm, but that still doesn't give them some kind of deep, essential connection. It just means that they pile high fae corpses from time to time, much as the Dragon-Blooded themselves do when the fae invade Creation (likely a notably rarer event in this edition, since the devs learned from the former, unendingly-reproducing model of the fae in prior editions, and were putting a clamp down on it back in the Fair Folk errata for 2.5e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:31:55-07:00","id":981508,"title":"","content":"While it'll never come to be, I've also always dreamed of Lunars being more tied to the Wyld, rather than less tied. But I also think being 'more tied' doesn't mean they should only be useful in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> If I was to design Lunars, I'd shift away from animals and the like, and focus on the chaos - they change shape because they have no permanency, because they embrace that they can have many forms, not because of a sacred connection to animals. Lunars in my design would be terrifying and potentially destabilizing entities, who do impossible things by turning off the logic and laws of the world. Think the 2e SMA Quicksilver Hands of Dreams (though mostly at smaller levels, except at high essence I guess.). They would turn parts of Creation into Wyld storms, just for a little bit, and remove Fate from their tiny army so that they can win ten to one against the Realm's army they were 'fated' to lose to. Their armies would be able to fly not because they created a hand crafted army with ships and etc like a solar, but because they removed the idea of 'humans can't fly' from existence for awhile.<br /> <br /> They would be utterly and completely terrifying to Sidereals, who rely on Creation and stability. They would be weapons created to attack the world bodies of the Primordials, and the ultimate rejection of the world they made. During the first age the whole Lunar/Solar bond thing would have been a willing thing, Solars helping to 'ground' their Lunar partner, keep their Chaos in check via their Order. Now without it, you get what are basically freeholds in Creation - Ma-Ha-Suchi isn't raising an army by fucking goat people/fucking people as a goat, he just has turned his entire home into this massively mutating Wyld Zone, and everyone who ventures into it becomes a terrifying monster man.<br /> <br /> A Lunar crafter would turn soup into a sword in an instant, would be capable of causing a forest to grow into a manse all on its own, would turn silk cloth into something as hard as steel. A Lunar warrior would bypass someone's guard by altering which direction their arm was moving instantly, or fire a dozen arrows at once that the wind all happened to carry to their target. A Lunar socialite would be a haunting enchanting beauty or terror, along the lines of a Fae, able to cloud the mind in a haze with words.<br /> <br /> <br /> But unfortunately, the Devs and many players prefer the 'sacred animal' approach to Lunars, and want to keep them tied to Werewolf stylings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 10-04-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:37:28-07:00","id":981512,"title":"","content":"It strikes me that Lunars and Dragon-Blooded don't necessarily need to be as strong as Solars to be interesting. They just need to not suck.<br /> <br /> Like, if you think about 1e trying to establish itself and give a vision of the world via mechanics, you can see how Dragon-Blooded, almost accidentally gigs hatred a bit in the sense that they felt the need to specifically make their powers worse than Solars.<br /> <br /> The sense I've gotten from reading discussions and listening to interviews, the benefit of another new edition is to look at that retrospectively and try to more fully realize the Dragon-Blooded as mechanically interesting without an explicit design goal of demonstrating them as second-fiddle to Celestials.<br /> <br /> I mean, we still know that a Dragon-Blooded can't reach the heights of power a Solar can, but that doesn't mean that the Dragon-Blooded are just left in the mud, you know?<br /> <br /> Lunars have the more complicated issue of how their first book came out in a messy way, but it doesn't mean they can't enact a similar notion. Read anything that Morke or Holden have said about Lunars and it's clear as day that they're fans of Lunars, so I certainly expect that, free of things like the Knack problem, they'll be able to explore mechanics of Lunars without just making them Silver Solars or Not As Good. If anything, I get the sense one should focus on method rather than totally fixating on power when looking at the difference in how a Lunar handles a problem versus a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-04-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:46:28-07:00","id":981523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981508#post981508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it'll never come to be, I've also always dreamed of Lunars being more tied to the Wyld, rather than less tied. But I also think being 'more tied' doesn't mean they should only be useful in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> If I was to design Lunars, I'd shift away from animals and the like, and focus on the chaos - they change shape because they have no permanency, because they embrace that they can have many forms, not because of a sacred connection to animals. Lunars in my design would be terrifying and potentially destabilizing entities, who do impossible things by turning off the logic and laws of the world. Think the 2e SMA Quicksilver Hands of Dreams (though mostly at smaller levels, except at high essence I guess.). They would turn parts of Creation into Wyld storms, just for a little bit, and remove Fate from their tiny army so that they can win ten to one against the Realm's army they were 'fated' to lose to. Their armies would be able to fly not because they created a hand crafted army with ships and etc like a solar, but because they removed the idea of 'humans can't fly' from existence for awhile.<br /> <br /> They would be utterly and completely terrifying to Sidereals, who rely on Creation and stability. They would be weapons created to attack the world bodies of the Primordials, and the ultimate rejection of the world they made. During the first age the whole Lunar/Solar bond thing would have been a willing thing, Solars helping to 'ground' their Lunar partner, keep their Chaos in check via their Order. Now without it, you get what are basically freeholds in Creation - Ma-Ha-Suchi isn't raising an army by fucking goat people/fucking people as a goat, he just has turned his entire home into this massively mutating Wyld Zone, and everyone who ventures into it becomes a terrifying monster man.<br /> <br /> <br /> But unfortunately, the Devs and many players prefer the 'sacred animal' approach to Lunars, and want to keep them tied to Werewolf stylings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't sound much like Lunars, honestly.<br /> But it does sound like a good basis for one of the new splats they're going to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:23:43-07:00","id":981551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981508#post981508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it'll never come to be, I've also always dreamed of Lunars being more tied to the Wyld, rather than less tied. But I also think being 'more tied' doesn't mean they should only be useful in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> If I was to design Lunars, I'd shift away from animals and the like, and focus on the chaos - they change shape because they have no permanency, because they embrace that they can have many forms, not because of a sacred connection to animals. Lunars in my design would be terrifying and potentially destabilizing entities, who do impossible things by turning off the logic and laws of the world. Think the 2e SMA Quicksilver Hands of Dreams (though mostly at smaller levels, except at high essence I guess.). They would turn parts of Creation into Wyld storms, just for a little bit, and remove Fate from their tiny army so that they can win ten to one against the Realm's army they were 'fated' to lose to. Their armies would be able to fly not because they created a hand crafted army with ships and etc like a solar, but because they removed the idea of 'humans can't fly' from existence for awhile.<br /> <br /> They would be utterly and completely terrifying to Sidereals, who rely on Creation and stability. They would be weapons created to attack the world bodies of the Primordials, and the ultimate rejection of the world they made. During the first age the whole Lunar/Solar bond thing would have been a willing thing, Solars helping to 'ground' their Lunar partner, keep their Chaos in check via their Order. Now without it, you get what are basically freeholds in Creation - Ma-Ha-Suchi isn't raising an army by fucking goat people/fucking people as a goat, he just has turned his entire home into this massively mutating Wyld Zone, and everyone who ventures into it becomes a terrifying monster man.<br /> <br /> <br /> But unfortunately, the Devs and many players prefer the 'sacred animal' approach to Lunars, and want to keep them tied to Werewolf stylings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I agree with you quite a lot, here, but let me expand on it. Purely whiteboarding follows.<br /> <br /> Lunars adapt themselves.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Lunars in the mundane wilderness adapt to that wilderness. Animals, plants, barbarians. Rain, fog, snow, oceans, grasslands, forest.<br /> Lunars in the Wyld adapt to the Wyld. Stories, waypoints, hobgoblins, unshaped things. Places that don't make sense. Places that invade your nightmares.<br /> Lunars in the city adapt to the city. Buildings, gangs, commerce, bureaucracies. Politics, intrigue, skullduggery.<br /> Lunars on the battlefield adapt to the battlefield. Armies, mud, blood, gore, and War. <br /> Lunars in Yu-Shan adapt to Yu-Shan. (The Usurpation Sids were strangely <i>lucky</i> to be able to ferret them out)<br /> Lunars working alongside with Solars adapt to the Solars. The same (to the shock of everybody in the age of sorrows) goes for the Solaroids. It might also go for Sids, Dragon-blooded, or others. <br /> <br /> [[ At low levels of Essence, a young Lunar may gain Shapes, Survival, Bureaucracy, War, etc. related Charms or Knacks that let them adapt to where they are or what's going on. It's long lasting (scene or so) and comes at the expense of being adapted to other areas at the same time. In the case of working with the Wyld, other Exalted, etc, it functions by enabling pack-tactics coordination, or by borrowing Charms or magic, or taking them by hunt or challenge. It might replace the concept of Lunar Fury, in that being in a battle is pretty much a Fury styled adaptation. It might also replace the Solar-Lunar bond, in that adapting to other Exalted is similar. ]]</div> <br /> Lunars adapt their surroundings.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">At middle levels of Essence, a Lunar may share the benefits of their adaptations with their allies:<br /> Friends instinctively sidestep hazards in the wilderness, and resist (or shape!) the mutating influence of the Wyld. <br /> Allied battle groups hide in the forest or the snow as if they've evaporated into nothing. <br /> Allies seem to bolster from the Lunar's amazing stamina and speed as they march, and never seem to be harmed by the weather.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a Lunar at this level may choose two, eventually three or more adaptations at the same time:<br /> A Lunar battling in the Wyld matches their own martial puissance with instinctive use of the strange terrain.<br /> Investigating an overgrown city, the Lunar is a shadow lurking equally well among the buildings and the jungle.<br /> </div> Lunars adapt the world.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">At the highest levels of (playable) Essence, a Lunar may change their present environment in ways that match another.<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi has his Wyld zone, exactly as you mentioned, but he might create one in a city or on a battlefield.<br /> Friendly battle groups rally out of the population of a city at the Lunar's call. <br /> A vast wilderness may hide a shortcut through a Waypoint to cross the whole distance.<br /> The tight grasp of an Unshaped may be forced into the purview of Destiny.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's easy to poke holes in this, but I think with some evolution it would be pretty fun and iconic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:50:12-07:00","id":981629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981508#post981508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it'll never come to be, I've also always dreamed of Lunars being more tied to the Wyld, rather than less tied. But I also think being 'more tied' doesn't mean they should only be useful in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> If I was to design Lunars, I'd shift away from animals and the like, and focus on the chaos - they change shape because they have no permanency, because they embrace that they can have many forms, not because of a sacred connection to animals. Lunars in my design would be terrifying and potentially destabilizing entities, who do impossible things by turning off the logic and laws of the world. Think the 2e SMA Quicksilver Hands of Dreams (though mostly at smaller levels, except at high essence I guess.). They would turn parts of Creation into Wyld storms, just for a little bit, and remove Fate from their tiny army so that they can win ten to one against the Realm's army they were 'fated' to lose to. Their armies would be able to fly not because they created a hand crafted army with ships and etc like a solar, but because they removed the idea of 'humans can't fly' from existence for awhile.<br /> <br /> They would be utterly and completely terrifying to Sidereals, who rely on Creation and stability. They would be weapons created to attack the world bodies of the Primordials, and the ultimate rejection of the world they made. During the first age the whole Lunar/Solar bond thing would have been a willing thing, Solars helping to 'ground' their Lunar partner, keep their Chaos in check via their Order. Now without it, you get what are basically freeholds in Creation - Ma-Ha-Suchi isn't raising an army by fucking goat people/fucking people as a goat, he just has turned his entire home into this massively mutating Wyld Zone, and everyone who ventures into it becomes a terrifying monster man.<br /> <br /> A Lunar crafter would turn soup into a sword in an instant, would be capable of causing a forest to grow into a manse all on its own, would turn silk cloth into something as hard as steel. A Lunar warrior would bypass someone's guard by altering which direction their arm was moving instantly, or fire a dozen arrows at once that the wind all happened to carry to their target. A Lunar socialite would be a haunting enchanting beauty or terror, along the lines of a Fae, able to cloud the mind in a haze with words.<br /> <br /> <br /> But unfortunately, the Devs and many players prefer the 'sacred animal' approach to Lunars, and want to keep them tied to Werewolf stylings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This level of mutabillity sounds like Lunars are something entirely of the Wyld. As in, more in line with the faeries and the Eternal revolutionary than with any current Exalted (or, ironically, like what I've heard of Sids as- very random and borderline nonesensical). And that could be an exalt type! But I'd still like a wild man exalted. An Enkidu to the Solar Gilgamesh (unless we decided Enkidu was a solar, just with survival supernal or athletics supernal).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:23:39-07:00","id":981694,"title":"","content":"@ KittyEmpress, your idea sounds a bit like TAW + Getimians really. <br /> <br /> (In a sense I think you would really need to design a group like that pretty carefully, if they're set up to be oppositional to something else that makes another splat cool (Fate) because there is a risk of both of them undermining each other. If the Sidereals are about disruptions from Fate being insane and pointless and a barrier to using the consistent rules of reality for real progress and real binding choices and high magic, and the anti-Fate splat are about how Fate's all a pointless constraint, then there is a risk of them both seeming uncool, esp. if you're all about how each one is cowering in the direction of the other, and are terrified by each other, rendering each other cowards in the eyes of the audience. But it seems to me that's what the developers are trying to make work with Getimians (an anti-Fate disruptive group), so there's that thing that they clearly agree it's worth trying.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:22:26-07:00","id":981774,"title":"","content":"KittyEmpress, your idea sounds like a little like TAW + Getimians, but also like they're native to the Wyld, not Creation.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, any splat that's wholly of the Wyld is inimical to Creation and a threat to Reality itself. The Wyld is inherently corrosive and constantly dissolving the edges of Creation, and will completely obliterate Reality if not fought non-stop. Whatever other roles the Exalted hosts had or didn't have, they were meant to protect Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:12:57-07:00","id":981863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981512#post981512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I get the sense one should focus on method rather than totally fixating on power\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Really this could be said of any splat in the gameline. And the gameline itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:54:36-07:00","id":981897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981863#post981863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really this could be said of any splat in the gameline. And the gameline itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it seems like focusing on the idea of being as powerful as x or y (or Solars) is an exercise in frustration. Especially because Solars are established as a pinnacle, we really ought to leave aside the idea of comparing everything with them so we aren't upset when other things fall short, but rather think about what makes this thing in particular interesting. Like do Lunars use shapeshifting to tackle all problems? Are their Charms about emulating animals or about emulating some kind of raw Attribute-oriented principle of action? Is that interesting as a methodological foil to the refined Ability mastery focus of Solars? Et al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:19:23-07:00","id":982107,"title":"","content":"Also, focusing on power is really dull.<br /> That's how we got Silver Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:48:13-07:00","id":982122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=982107#post982107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, focusing on power is really dull.<br /> That's how we got Silver Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, within limits.<br /> <br /> When the potential of a whole splat is to bask in the glory of their betters, it's beyond those limits. <br /> <br /> That's why I phrase it like I do, above. Playing well and staying in theme should result in parity with other well-played splats' characters kept in theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:27:44-07:00","id":984596,"title":"","content":"\u200bLot of good posts in this thread, glad I'm following it. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=980585#post980585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have only played 3E exalted and do not carry any knowledge of the previous editions or of W:tA either although I know what it is.<br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> Anyway as an ignorant of previous settings gamer that was my impression of my read through of the 3E core book in relation to Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is both a pro and con for you Drakor, it lets you look with fresher eyes than some of us and thus have less bias when you come at the new material. The con is that not only is there a huge backlog of material that will take Onyx a good 10+ years to catch up with (or so I guess) but you might actually like some things better from previous editions. Overall though, IMHO 3E is significantly better and richer with the franchise.<br /> <br /> FWIW though, my favorite 2E series were the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?keywords=exalted+compass++of+celestial&amp;manufacturers_id=1&amp;x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=&amp;artist=&amp;pfrom=&amp;pto=\" target=\"_blank\">Celestial Directions</a> books, did a lot to portray the world in greater depth though before you buy them on impulse, it does have the inherit flaw of WW of assuming you've bought everything else. Still, if it ever goes on sale, its a good buy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=980649#post980649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lunars have to be in someway inextricably linked to the Wyld. Their Patron has strong links to it. And not just as someone who battles it but someone who courts it and flirts with it. Sometime's she is at the UCS side fighting it back and sometimes he is frollicking in the oceans of madness and I think Lunars should have this side to them.<br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> ]I guess I'm just a bit a cynical of there being a type of Exalted who's patron has strong links to the Wyld, who have a history of both battling the Wyld and using it as a refuge, who represent themes of animalism, shape changing and &quot;barbarian&quot; culture (where Wyld Barbarian, Wyld beasts and Wyld mutations are all strongly linked to these themes), who have moonsilver tattoos specifically to help them both mutate in creation and hold form in the wyld, now have nothing whatsoever to do with the Wyld. It seems to take lots away without adding anything to me. While it is true Raksha are creatures of the Wyld I dont see them treading on each others conceptual space. Liminals don't tread on Abyssals space yet interacting at the edges of the Underworld as Lunars do with the Wyld works. The Lunar's have close links to the Wyld than any other Exalt type (raskha are not exalts) I fail to see what is gained by rewarding this. I get that the benefits of being able to participate in Shaping combat was pretty limited and difficult to use. So re-imagining how the Wyld informs their aesthetic and mechanics is key but I think severing that tie is out of context for them and takes away an interesting arena for story and development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully I would disagree. Considering we were told Luna's participation in the war against the primordials <i>required</i> the US to expressly spare Gaia or Luna would have nothing to do with his scheme. Gaia was/is Luna's &quot;soulmate&quot; and given that Creation is essentially, Gaia, the nature of the Wyld is to erode/consume Creation and thus Gaia no? So I don't see a celestial entity being all that keen on the notion of being playfully immersed in its depths or taking refuge in something that literally <i>unmakes its most cherished of lovers</i>. <br /> <br /> The entire Wyld this/that lovefest of 2E is also something I found to be contradictory, if anything the animism of &quot;barbarian cultures&quot; is far more natural than those same cultures looking at the Wyld as something they learn to like/embrace. IMHO spirit totems not only makes for better rule clarity, but is something most people can identify with more readily than some overly romanticized prose of embracing the so called virtues of pure chaos. <br /> <br /> That will perhaps mark me as close minded or staid or...whatever, but oh well. 2E also had Lunars <i>mating</i> with beasts to create offspring, something which I thought was in dreadful taste, causing me to me to takel that entire edition's theme/background and toss it in the shredder. While my old mates and I did a rework of what Lunars powers/abilities were to a extent, it was the background that had me saying &quot;Guys, none of WW's material applies, read this instead&quot; as I dropped a 30 some page handout infront of them.<br /> <br /> In breif, I would be delighted if Onyx gave the whole Wyld hugging themes of 2E the solid kick in the ass it deserves and embrace a more animistic theme, though admittedly I may be overly biased due to my history with W;TA and I'm obviously someone who didn't like the way Lunars were presented, while others loved them. To each his own.<br /> <br /> That said, if I ever found myself near your table I'd be quite interested in observing how you handle this sort of thing, you had some interesting Lunar themes in that post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=981774#post981774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KittyEmpress, your idea sounds like a little like TAW + Getimians, but also like they're native to the Wyld, not Creation.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, any splat that's wholly of the Wyld is inimical to Creation and a threat to Reality itself. The Wyld is inherently corrosive and constantly dissolving the edges of Creation, and will completely obliterate Reality if not fought non-stop. Whatever other roles the Exalted hosts had or didn't have, they were meant to protect Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad I'm not the only one who has this perception. But I have to ask, while I was able to find what the Getimians are (I completely missed any reference to them in any of the various books, but then again I'm not terribly conversant with the 2E Sidereals and their various exotica) I have no clue what &quot;TAW&quot; refers to. Someone care to enlighten me?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:44:44-07:00","id":984650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker1728</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=984596#post984596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> I'm glad I'm not the only one who has this perception. But I have to ask, while I was able to find what the Getimians are (I completely missed any reference to them in any of the various books, but then again I'm not terribly conversant with the 2E Sidereals and their various exotica) I have no clue what &quot;TAW&quot; refers to. Someone care to enlighten me?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>TAW: Terrifying Argent(ardent?) witches. I found them in the 1st edition outcaste book. Really really cool and creepy dragonblooded cult thing.<br /> <br /> Getmetians: New exalt type coming in 3e. The taoist rebels to the Sideral's shinto/confusican priests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:38:04-07:00","id":984674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker1728</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=984596#post984596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> I'm glad I'm not the only one who has this perception. But I have to ask, while I was able to find what the Getimians are (I completely missed any reference to them in any of the various books, but then again I'm not terribly conversant with the 2E Sidereals and their various exotica) I have no clue what &quot;TAW&quot; refers to. Someone care to enlighten me?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>TAW, Terrifying Argent Witches, were an attempt to change what Lunars did in 2e. They basically just ended up with Silver Sidereals and Infernals, treating Attributes as high-concept categories akin to Sidereal sutras or Yozis instead of as tangible qualities related to an effect. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/417202-lunars-and-taw\">Here's the last thread we had on them</a>, I think (it got difficult to keep track over the years). They're a point of contention because a lot of supporters were agitating for their inclusion as canon in the new edition. Thankfully, the developers were having none of that (not that they legally could, since, you know, fan projects and all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-09-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T22:46:39-07:00","id":984755,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11835_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11835\" data-vbnamecard=\"11835\">Epee102</a> &amp; Saur Ops Specicialt<br /> <br /> Thanks guys, particularly for the link. After reading it and the thread I hope the 3E learns a lot from past mistakes and with no slight intended at the authors of the TAW but definitely glad to hear they're not a thing to see official embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:02:37-07:00","id":984804,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I agree with the barbarian themes as an intrinsic part of Lunarness. After all, they were created (presumably) in Yu-Shan, and for an era much longer than the Age of Sorrows were welcome there. <br /> <br /> They primarily exist at the edges of Creation because they were pushed there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:55:51-07:00","id":984905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=984804#post984804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I agree with the barbarian themes as an intrinsic part of Lunarness. After all, they were created (presumably) in Yu-Shan, and for an era much longer than the Age of Sorrows were welcome there.<br /> <br /> They primarily exist at the edges of Creation because they were pushed there.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they were created, the gods lived on the Blessed Isle. When the Lunars were created, they also probably still accomplished their feats by gaining monstrous features with shapeshifting, so they wouldn't be very genteel when in action. Grapple someone with gorilla or bear arms, rip into them with moonsilver claws, feel their heartbeat with Lorenzini's ampullae... what comes up for performing tasks tends to go against that grain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:52:36-07:00","id":985011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=984804#post984804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I agree with the barbarian themes as an intrinsic part of Lunarness. After all, they were created (presumably) in Yu-Shan, and for an era much longer than the Age of Sorrows were welcome there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking over developer comments from over the years, it looks to me like you could have both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:24:05-07:00","id":985032,"title":"","content":"I think they tend to embrace the notion that Lunars are visceral and raw rather than being politically barbaric or anything like that. In the First Age they weren't barbarians, but they were dangerous and raw in the night in a way a Solar might be more refined in their application of Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:16:08-07:00","id":985211,"title":"","content":"A major problem I always had with 2e &amp; 1e Lunars is that I felt most of their charms were athematic to how Luna was portrayed. If you were to look at them and attempt to recreate what Luna was like, you'd expect a primal beast-goddess, probably- But Luna doesn't really have a strong Animal theme to my knowledge. I can't even recall her ever taking the form of an animal; her primary aspects were all humanoid.<br /> <br /> Sure people sort of waved at it and said, &quot;Somewhat Something Gaia.&quot;, but that never really seemed like a satisfying answer to me.<br /> <br /> And, in general, the whole visceral and raw theme never really seemed, &quot;Luna&quot; to me either. I can accept that's a change that's going to happen, but I only hope there's a reasonable integration between Lunar themes and what Luna is like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:24:38-07:00","id":985764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker1728</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=984596#post984596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bRespectfully I would disagree. Considering we were told Luna's participation in the war against the primordials <i>required</i> the US to expressly spare Gaia or Luna would have nothing to do with his scheme. Gaia was/is Luna's &quot;soulmate&quot; and given that Creation is essentially, Gaia, the nature of the Wyld is to erode/consume Creation and thus Gaia no? So I don't see a celestial entity being all that keen on the notion of being playfully immersed in its depths or taking refuge in something that literally <i>unmakes its most cherished of lovers</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Creation is not Gaia's body. It never has been in canon, although some writers imported that assumption from Werewolf. That resulted in confusing statements in some books, but they were errors that didn't get caught by the editors.<br /> <br /> <br /> To me, Luna's connection to the Wyld isn't about being from the Wyld and inimical to Creation. She is (er, was, before getting addicted to the Games of Divinity) one of the entities who most defended Creation from the Wyld. Rather, she is a being who can in some way relate to things from the Wyld, who can wrench energy from the Wyld and transform it into something positive for Creation. She plays games with Raksha, but she also kills them, and sometimes transforms their Essence into truculee, little gods tied to Creation instead of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Analogy: If Creation is the Netherlands, and the Wyld is the sea, the raksha are horrifying tentacled things that keep crawling out of the ocean and toppling the dams that keep the Netherlands above water. Luna is the bazooka-wielding*, scuba-diving marine biologist, and Gaia is the dam engineer.<br /> <br /> Now, Luna <i><b>is</b></i> also a shapeshifting eldritch horror, but she's a <i><b>Creation-born</b></i> shapeshifting eldritch horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Luna's bazooka totally works underwater, btw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:21:28-07:00","id":985842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=985764#post985764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, Luna's connection to the Wyld isn't about being from the Wyld and inimical to Creation. She is (er, was, before getting addicted to the Games of Divinity) one of the entities who most defended Creation from the Wyld. Rather, she is a being who can in some way relate to things from the Wyld, who can wrench energy from the Wyld and transform it into something positive for Creation. She plays games with Raksha, but she also kills them, and sometimes transforms their Essence into truculee, little gods tied to Creation instead of the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truculee aren't going to be a thing in EX3, though. It kind of goes hand in hand with how drastically different the Fair Folk will be working, I think, with an equal concern of how to focus everything primarily on Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:27:23-07:00","id":986023,"title":"","content":"I liked the concept of the Truculee but I thought the execution stole a place a Fair Folk PC could occupy and hold more trust in a mixed game than the default &quot;I've decided to be a hero! but don't worry I won't turn on you until I'm <i>really</i> bored with it&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:38:36-07:00","id":986156,"title":"","content":"Thinking about this topic lately, I've taken a liking to a different approach.<br /> <br /> Solars are the Big Damn Heroes. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are the seers and powers behind the throne.<br /> <br /> Lunars are the intrinsic opposition, for both heroes and villains. They're the monster that stalks the woods, but they're also the beast who terrorizes the Wyld. They're the threat that stimulates growth and preparation, and the outsider who visits but never quite belongs. They wander, bringing trouble to hubris and ruin to vanity and war to the passive. Sometimes they're the Robin who's got Batman's back, and sometimes the Joker who makes Bats what he has to be.<br /> <br /> Ask a young Lunar, and he will explain that the Lunar Exaltation comes to those who guard their own truths and challenge orthodoxies.<br /> <br /> Ask an elder, and she will laugh and explain Moonsilver Philosophy: embody the Orichalcum of Excellence in the face of complacency; rend the wicked with the Soulsteel of Endings; choose your own destiny with Starmetal of your own will; burn away all that is false with the Vitriol of rage; carve the love of Creation in grand monuments of Jade. <br /> <br /> Even in the First Age, the Lunars first warned of the dangerous excesses and unchecked tyrannies. At the Usurpation, they howled in rage and tried to defend what was left. <br /> <br /> In the Age of Sorrows, some believe that the Lunar Anathema make unholy bargains with the Raksha. They are wrong. It is the Raksha who must (ever so elegantly) bow and beg bargains with the Lunars, for Lunar will challenges even the mightiest stories of the Unshaped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:39:05-07:00","id":986185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=986023#post986023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the concept of the Truculee but I thought the execution stole a place a Fair Folk PC could occupy and hold more trust in a mixed game than the default &quot;I've decided to be a hero! but don't worry I won't turn on you until I'm <i>really</i> bored with it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta be honest, I'm not sure why Fair Folk were ever made playable if they're meant to be invariably and immutably antagonistic to all Creation. I think most groups I've played with would react to that sample character pitch with violence, because I mean really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:35:52-07:00","id":986305,"title":"","content":"Bedlam is a serious problem that pitch is just being rather blunt about it, like an Abyssal going in with &quot;I sold out to the enemies of Creation but now I'm having second thoughts so my dark fate will bring down the world anyway starting with the things I care about, can I join your group?&quot;<br /> <br /> But I do think it was a mistake to make the Mountain Folk and Truculee their own species rather than Fair Folk with a loyalty towards Creation, as the former canonically were until Exalted: the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to think that we very easily could've had Fae that were aligned to the Realm and would've nicely facilitated mixed games there until they became to all intents and purposes something completely different in a way that overshadowed their existing relationship with the Realm by giving them their own environment and problems that are mostly there to distract them from the rest of the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-13-2016, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:50:36-07:00","id":986317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=986156#post986156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about this topic lately, I've taken a liking to a different approach.<br /> <br /> Solars are the Big Damn Heroes.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are the seers and powers behind the throne.<br /> <br /> Lunars are the intrinsic opposition, for both heroes and villains. They're the monster that stalks the woods, but they're also the beast who terrorizes the Wyld. They're the threat that stimulates growth and preparation, and the outsider who visits but never quite belongs. They wander, bringing trouble to hubris and ruin to vanity and war to the passive. Sometimes they're the Robin who's got Batman's back, and sometimes the Joker who makes Bats what he has to be.<br /> <br /> <b>Ask a young Lunar, and he will explain that the Lunar Exaltation comes to those who guard their own truths and challenge orthodoxies.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f4Mc-NYPHaQ\" target=\"_blank\">Not quite.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ask an elder, and she will laugh and explain Moonsilver Philosophy: embody the Orichalcum of Excellence in the face of complacency; rend the wicked with the Soulsteel of Endings; choose your own destiny with Starmetal of your own will; burn away all that is false with the Vitriol of rage; carve the love of Creation in grand monuments of Jade.<br /> <br /> Even in the First Age, the Lunars first warned of the dangerous excesses and unchecked tyrannies. At the Usurpation, they howled in rage and tried to defend what was left.<br /> <br /> In the Age of Sorrows, some believe that the Lunar Anathema make unholy bargains with the Raksha. They are wrong. It is the Raksha who must (ever so elegantly) bow and beg bargains with the Lunars, for Lunar will challenges even the mightiest stories of the Unshaped. </div> </div> </div>I don't know if shaped vs unshaped is going to be quite the struggle that we're going to be getting. The hannya have their own designation as a thing in the Wyld, and there will probably be more where they came from. Meanwhile, the Lunars probably aren't going to be doing any favors for the raksha or their servants. Lead the Realm into them perhaps, and them into the Realm, but I'm not seeing a friendly interaction shaping up, obsequious-acting fae or otherwise..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:27:16-07:00","id":987886,"title":"","content":"I think a Dev said that the argentim and aurichim are gone in 3E, but the truculee may stay canon.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I also never understood the appeal of playing a raksha, but I figured they were playable for the same reason loyalist Abyssals are playable. I can't conceive of a faerie ever being capable of genuine loyalty to Creation (or to anything else), but some players like destroying Creation, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:52:46-07:00","id":987897,"title":"","content":"The Fair Folk changed since their earliest appearance. They went from what you have in the 1e core - &quot;However, many of the Fair Folk have entered the world and have taken onshape to do so. Most of these beings are tricksters and hunters of men, but some coexist with mortals, ruling them as lords in some places and living among them as citizens in others&quot; - to the 3e core - &quot;Those Fair Folk who venture into reality survive by eating dreams or souls. Many claim to seek the dissolution of the world, though a few seem happy to play at life among mortals&quot; (and actually most post 1e core, pre-3e core stuff went harder in the direction of insane, inimicable Fair Folk than the 3e core).<br /> <br /> That changed happened quite early in 1e actually (and many would say for the best!), making the Fair Folk less immediately playable as the strange, otherworldly sometime allies of the Exalted and mankind, but Graceful Wicked Masks and Fair Folk as playable were planned before that. <br /> <br /> So when Exalted: The Fair Folk happened it reoriented The Fair Folk to be the players of mysterious world shaping games and wars in the Wyld, so you could totally play down the aspects of destroying reality and preying on humans for courtly infighting among insane, but charming and courtly, Dancers At The End of Time sorts. I think it's an appealing venue to play about in, provided people like playing charming and stylish amoral characters, though that system for playing the reality shaping games and war of the Fair Folk in the Wyld was probably too complex for what it tried to do, being a repurposed multiplication of the 1e combat system (multiple health tracks and all) with a lot of heavy abstraction. It remains to be seen how much of that will survive!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:30:45-07:00","id":988096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=984650#post984650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TAW: Terrifying Argent(ardent?) witches. I found them in the 1st edition outcaste book. Really really cool and creepy dragonblooded cult thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of the Forest Witches, possibly the first major contribution Borgstrom made to Exalted! Wonder if they'll be revisited in 3E, and, if so, how they might change?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A major problem I always had with 2e &amp; 1e Lunars is that I felt most of their charms were athematic to how Luna was portrayed. If you were to look at them and attempt to recreate what Luna was like, you'd expect a primal beast-goddess, probably- But Luna doesn't really have a strong Animal theme to my knowledge. I can't even recall her ever taking the form of an animal; her primary aspects were all humanoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Luna *is* in charge of the Bureau of Nature, which handles all of Creation's animals. And as of Glories, her shapeshifting involved every type of animal as well as the &quot;Chthonic Baara&quot;, sort of a massive chimerical Superbeast! It's also established that one of her most prevalent forms is of a battle-crazed berserker barbarian woman, so she has the &quot;viscereal rawness&quot; down...s/he's pretty versatile like that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: BTW, Lunars have been mating with animals to breed beastmen since 1E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 10-15-2016, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T21:32:51-07:00","id":988119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988096#post988096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Luna *is* in charge of the Bureau of Nature, which handles all of Creation's animals. And as of Glories, her shapeshifting involved every type of animal as well as the &quot;Chthonic Baara&quot;, sort of a massive chimerical Superbeast! It's also established that one of her most prevalent forms is of a battle-crazed berserker barbarian woman, so she has the &quot;viscereal rawness&quot; down...s/he's pretty versatile like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's generally just easier to clobber people with the developer statements. I remember the dark days of earlier 2012.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: BTW, Lunars have been mating with animals to breed beastmen since 1E. </div> </div> </div>But quite possibly not this edition, since there have been a number of other ways that beastfolk happen and the myth of the Minotaur didn't really have a real Lunar-y figure in it, so why make it tied to them? Even DBT isn't really reason enough, because they generally don't park themselves in it, and even if they do, they can change out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:13:57-07:00","id":988151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988119#post988119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But quite possibly not this edition, since there have been a number of other ways that beastfolk happen and the myth of the Minotaur didn't really have a real Lunar-y figure in it, so why make it tied to them? Even DBT isn't really reason enough, because they generally don't park themselves in it, and even if they do, they can change out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a power that mutates a Lunar's human followers, who must engage in a ritual hunt wherein they each track and skin a particular type of animal, then wear its pelt in an ecstatic dance during which the Lunar's power morphs them into beastman shape? This could be permanent, but maybe it being temporary would make them extra dependent on their Lunar master. But would this best be a Charm or Spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T08:28:26-07:00","id":988258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988151#post988151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a power that mutates a Lunar's human followers, who must engage in a ritual hunt wherein they each track and skin a particular type of animal, then wear its pelt in an ecstatic dance during which the Lunar's power morphs them into beastman shape? This could be permanent, but maybe it being temporary would make them extra dependent on their Lunar master. But would this best be a Charm or Spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually going to go with spell, because we have a statement of intent about the Lunars changing themselves to change the world, not changing others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:50:38-07:00","id":988323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988258#post988258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually going to go with spell, because we have a statement of intent about the Lunars changing themselves to change the world, not changing others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:06:53-07:00","id":988328,"title":"","content":"I'm not so into the reasoning about changing others vs not changing others, but it does feel more like a spell to me in its scale and form. Feels quite sorcerous. I could imagine a variation which is less tightly ritualistic and overtly transformative and worked more on internal essence and skills being a Charm (but this doesn't really get us any closer to Beastfolk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:25:24-07:00","id":988358,"title":"","content":"I think Lunars should just be able to have beastfolk children based on any of their true forms, or any of their heart's-blood forms with extra work, without any bestiality. I really like the idea of beastfolk being their descendants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:43:31-07:00","id":988413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988358#post988358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lunars should just be able to have beastfolk children based on any of their true forms, or any of their heart's-blood forms with extra work, without any bestiality. I really like the idea of beastfolk being their descendants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally get behind Lunars being able to impregnate women with a child based on ANYTHING in their Heart's Blood library. The child would need to be a human-baby-sized beastfolk to be viably carried to term and born, of course, which limits the options. (Of course, Lunars could also impregnate <i>non-human</i> females.)<br /> <br /> The same Charm would let a Lunar conceive and give birth to anything from their Heart's Blood library, though given their own shapeshifting, they have greater variety of the sizes and shapes they can birth.<br /> <br /> They might also be able to conceive parthenogenetically. Ie: Without sex or sperm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:48:50-07:00","id":988419,"title":"","content":"On one hand the whole 'conceived' thing is interesting and kinda fits to fiction [that I don't really like] in that the Solar can raise their amazing armor through a few weeks of training, while a Lunar has to breed their army, and all things considered the Lunar's will look like freakish monsters. On the other hand, I hate the kinds of characters it encourages if they wanna play the Beastman Raising Lunar. No, we do not need more Rape Lunars, or Ravishing Lunars, or whatever you wanna call them, that use magical persuasion to breed armies of monsters with tons and tons of women who otherwise wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Parthenogenesis seems like it'd be a fun way to take it without tying the 'Lunar who Leads Beastmen' to having to have ways to have dozens upon dozens of babies,<br /> <br /> <br /> No matter what though, just like in NWoD vs OWoD, we need to fucking ditch the gross as hell, edgy beastiality shit. It's just gross. If we want Lunars to be the bestial exalts, I'd sure hope they were like Werewolf, not like Changing Breeds aka the worst WoD thing ever made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:10:25-07:00","id":988434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988419#post988419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand the whole 'conceived' thing is interesting and kinda fits to fiction [that I don't really like] in that the Solar can raise their amazing armor through a few weeks of training, while a Lunar has to breed their army</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars will still have Charisma/Intelligence-based training/teaching Charms. BETTER ones than before.<br /> <br /> They don't have to rely solely on breeding beastfolk. Or do it at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:33:36-07:00","id":988554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988434#post988434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars will still have Charisma/Intelligence-based training/teaching Charms. BETTER ones than before.<br /> <br /> They don't have to rely solely on breeding beastfolk. Or do it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly since Holden mentioned that the Wyld coming through and going poof* was the typical way of getting beastfolk.<br /> <br /> *Not to be confused with going pomf, which, just... no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:11:48-07:00","id":988644,"title":"","content":"Personally I love oWoD.<br /> <br /> Mating in human form with an animal, or in animal form with a human? YUCK. That's bestiality.<br /> <br /> But I think Lunars absolutely should be able to make yeddimfolk by shapeshifting into a yeddim and mating with a yeddim. I really don't understand the objection to this existing as an option. When you shapeshift, you <b><i>become that animal</i></b>. It's not an illusion, it's not a mind-game. You literally became a yeddim. You're a sapient yeddim with super magic powers and a human soul, but still a yeddim. Even moreso if the yeddim is a true form. To me that isn't bestiality. And for players who find any sex in their game uncomfortable there can be other options too. (see below)<br /> <br /> I really have a problem with beastfolk always or mostly being Wyld mutants. The Wyld is fundamentally inimical to Creation. Anything mutated by the Wyld is probably helping to destroy Creation or at least human civilization. So having the Lunars allies with Wyld mutants who want to destroy civilization or need to taint the land because they can't even survive in Creation, fundamentally makes them villains. That's going backwards to the 1E &quot;Lunars want to destroy cities and aqueducts and farming, Hulk smash.&quot; I really am not interested in Lunars as allies of the Fair Folk or out to destroy civilization, but that's probably what you have to do when your allies and armies have to be Wyld mutants.<br /> <br /> It also means that if you want to raise an army, you have to be out on the edge of the map. Lunar games should not be limited to those places. Lunars should be capable of functioning in cities, in the Scavenger Lands, in the Deshan, wherever Solars can go. Part of the appeal to shapeshifting and being so adaptable is being able to adapt to <b><i>anywhere</i></b>. So why tell Lunar players that if they go 500 miles from the edge of reality, suddenly all their resources are gone? That's crappy.<br /> <br /> Other ways to get beastfolk faster: Option #1 in my mind is the round up an army of beastfolk from the beastfolk who <b>are already around</b>. The 3E corebook has Prince Diamond helping some random wolffolk tribe and there's no mention of a Lunar anywhere in town (otherwise, the local Lunar probably would have explained to that river god what happens to gods who interfere with a Celestial's worshippers).<br /> <br /> Also, beastfolk shouldn't only be anthropomorphic animals. I like those, but what about hawkfolk who look like baselines but with the eyesight of hawks? Why not camelfolk who look human but need as little water as camels, without the hump? If you can use some Lunar equivalent of genesis crafting/Verdant Emptiness Endowment to infuse animal blood into adults, why not flyfolk who look human but have the <b><i>unbelievably fast</i></b> reflexes of flies? Holy crap, flyfolk would be a terror in battle!<br /> <br /> Lastly, Lunars in 3E have a policy of building armies of regular baseline humans, so that'll presumably be an option for PCs now. Yeah, there are a shitton of dispossessed and oppressed people in Creation, because the Realm is a horrible genocidal empire. Anyone a Solar can rally, a Lunar can also rally. Their Charms and methods will be different, presumably the results will differ in some way too. But the fictions says it can be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-17-2016, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:54:20-07:00","id":988665,"title":"","content":"The cosmetic details seem to be the main point of beastfolk. Calling somebody with high reflexes a hybrid between a human and a fly is really tenuous.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for beastiality, I think that if 15th century Iranians of all people can find graphic pictures of people having sex with animals for whatever purpose the person who drew it hand in mind for the readers, then it's good enough for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:12:03-07:00","id":988907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988644#post988644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I love oWoD.<br /> <br /> Mating in human form with an animal, or in animal form with a human? YUCK. That's bestiality.<br /> <br /> But I think Lunars absolutely should be able to make yeddimfolk by shapeshifting into a yeddim and mating with a yeddim. I really don't understand the objection to this existing as an option. When you shapeshift, you <b><i>become that animal</i></b>. It's not an illusion, it's not a mind-game. You literally became a yeddim. You're a sapient yeddim with super magic powers and a human soul, but still a yeddim. Even moreso if the yeddim is a true form. That is not bestiality, it's shapeshifting. And for players who find any sex uncomfortable there can be other options too. (see below)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just stick to sorcery for everyone. It seems like pretty much anyone could pull a Dr. Moreau, anyway, and, again, the minotaur didn't have any Lunar figures around to beget him. Just a woman, a bull, and the vengeful spite of the gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really have a big problem with beastfolk always or mostly being Wyld mutants. The Wyld is fundamentally inimical to Creation. Anything mutated by the Wyld is probably helping to destroy Creation or at least human civilization. So having the Lunars allies with soul-sucking Wyld mutants who want to destroy civilization or taint the land because they can't even survive in Creation, fundamentally makes them villains equal to the loyalist Abyssals in depravity. That's going back to the 1E &quot;Lunars want to destroy cities and aqueducts and farming, Hulk smash.&quot; I really am not interested in Lunars as allies of the Fair Folk or out to destroy civilization, but that's what you have to do when your allies and armies have to be Wyld mutants. </div> </div> </div>The Wyld isn't necessarily super-antagonistic, and the people that get altered aren't, either. Both are simply just strange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also means that if you want to raise an army, you have to be out on the edge of the map. Lunar games should not be limited to those places. Lunars should be capable of functioning in cities, in the Scavenger Lands, in the Deshan, wherever Solars can go. Part of the appeal to shapeshifting and being so adaptable is being able to adapt to <b><i>anywhere</i></b>. So why tell Lunar players that if they go 500 miles from the edge of reality, suddenly all their resources are gone? That's crappy. </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. There are probably a lot of pockets of beastfolk left when the Wyld overflowed the last time. There are also isolated pockets of chaos around Creation that have left legacies; one even exists in Nexus, of all places. The origin of the Lookshy rebel also indicates that some bits of Wyld might have been sealed into containers in the First Age. But then, that is only the most common way, not the only one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other ways to get beastfolk faster: Option #1 in my mind is the round up an army of beastfolk from the beastfolk who <b>are already around</b>. The 3E corebook has Prince Diamond helping some random wolffolk tribe and there's no mention of a Lunar anywhere in town (otherwise, the local Lunar probably would have explained to that river god what happens to gods who interfere with a Celestial's worshippers). </div> </div> </div>Likely left behind from what I just mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, beastfolk shouldn't only be anthropomorphic animals. I like those, but what about hawkfolk who look like baselines but with the eyesight of hawks? Why not camelfolk who look human but need as little water as camels, without the hump? If you can use some Lunar equivalent of genesis crafting/Verdant Emptiness Endowment to infuse animal blood into adults, why not flyfolk who look human but have the <b><i>unbelievably fast</i></b> reflexes of flies? Holy crap, flyfolk would be a terror in battle! </div> </div> </div>Beastfolk get their capabilities from those changes. Without the changes, they don't have them. Some might have more human faces, like one of Yena's Daughters who doesn't have a muzzle, but in that case they don't get some other benefits, such as, say, improved olfaction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:46:51-07:00","id":988926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=988644#post988644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think Lunars absolutely should be able to make yeddimfolk by shapeshifting into a yeddim and mating with a yeddim. I really don't understand the objection to this existing as an option. When you shapeshift, you <b><i>become that animal</i></b>. It's not an illusion, it's not a mind-game. You literally became a yeddim. You're a sapient yeddim with super magic powers and a human soul, but still a yeddim. Even moreso if the yeddim is a true form. To me that isn't bestiality. And for players who find any sex in their game uncomfortable there can be other options too. (see below)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the whole sapient element might be an issue. If you've got a sapient yeddim mating with a non-sapient yeddim, then it's a bit equivalent to a sapient human mating with a non-sapient human. Which is a bit like at odd with what at least some people think is good sexual ethics or icky. (Is sexual ethics even a term?). Not that this bothers me too much but trying to think about people who it might.<br /> <br /> You could always have &quot;When two Lunars love other very much... they turn into yeddim and birth a nation of yeddimpeople&quot; if people are not feelin' the sapient+non sapient thing, and I think that would be cool as a way for intra-Lunar marriages to happen actually. <br /> <br /> (Or another alternative is for Lunars to have children with natural Wyld created beastmen, stabilizing and washing away Wyld taint and still leaving them as beastmen.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:30:24-07:00","id":989041,"title":"","content":"I had somehow forgotten about Creation having Wyld Zone cancer, so yeah that isn't as much of a limit on Lunars. &gt;.&lt;<br /> Wyld mutants being generally inimical to everyone else and/or unable to live in stable Creation is still my perception, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> I get the idea of sapient + nonsapient as a general definition of bestiality, which makes sense. But I remember Werewolf making it clear that if you are literally a wolf, it's entirely possible to attract a nonsapient wolf to mate you without it being rape, by just sticking to the normal wolf courtship methods. That makes sense to me, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorcery being an option is good, though I think Lunars should have an easier time of it than random other Celestials, if only by having other methods available.<br /> And maybe using Lunar blood as a ritual component gives you extra Means to turn a bunch of followers into beastfolk, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:35:01-07:00","id":989115,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure any amount of ethical or philosophical musing on sapience and consent can really address the problem of &quot;Fuck this wolf or <s>the Earth will die</s> Chejop gonna git ya&quot;. Even setting aside all the setting/gameplay issues inherent to supersoldier eugenics programs...y'all know that creepy anime trope of &quot;Don't worry, she's actually a 7,000-year-old demon who just happens to LOOK like a prepubescent child, so it's okay to sexualize her&quot;? Because I kinda get the same vibe here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:52:07-07:00","id":989125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=989041#post989041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had somehow forgotten about Creation having Wyld Zone cancer, so yeah that isn't as much of a limit on Lunars. &gt;.&lt;<br /> Wyld mutants being generally inimical to everyone else and/or unable to live in stable Creation is still my perception, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to mutation mechanics, withering is heavily downplayed in EX3. There's only a single flaw as of yet that has to do with it, and it's purely a social penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get the idea of sapient + nonsapient as a general definition of bestiality, which makes sense. But I remember Werewolf making it clear that if you are literally a wolf, it's entirely possible to attract a nonsapient wolf to mate you without it being rape, by just sticking to the normal wolf courtship methods. That makes sense to me, too. </div> </div> </div>A fair number of characters in W:tA were wolfweres, though. Being with humans would probably feel weird for them. All Exalted, however, started out human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorcery being an option is good, though I think Lunars should have an easier time of it than random other Celestials, if only by having other methods available.<br /> And maybe using Lunar blood as a ritual component gives you extra Means to turn a bunch of followers into beastfolk, eh? </div> </div> </div>It's not likely so taxing a working that it would require any extra means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:15:55-07:00","id":989335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=989115#post989115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure any amount of ethical or philosophical musing on sapience and consent can really address the problem of &quot;Fuck this wolf or <s>the Earth will die</s> Chejop gonna git ya&quot;. Even setting aside all the setting/gameplay issues inherent to supersoldier eugenics programs...y'all know that creepy anime trope of &quot;Don't worry, she's actually a 7,000-year-old demon who just happens to LOOK like a prepubescent child, so it's okay to sexualize her&quot;? Because I kinda get the same vibe here.</div> </div> </div> </div>One possible way around that would be to take the knack from 2e which let you give animal traits to purely human-on-human children and make that a basic ability all Lunars have (maybe with the requirement that you have to have spent a lot of time in that form recently.)<br /> <br /> This has mythological basis, I think, and would fit into DB propaganda about Anathema - you got seduced by that handsome stranger from out of town, and nine months later you give birth to beastmen abominations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:37:41-07:00","id":989365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=989115#post989115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure any amount of ethical or philosophical musing on sapience and consent can really address the problem of &quot;Fuck this wolf or <s>the Earth will die</s> Chejop gonna git ya&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat sounds to me like transferring a lot of baggage that has nothing to do with this game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:02:29-08:00","id":999450,"title":"","content":"This has most likely already been addressed, but the thread was already tl;dr by the time I got here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I liked the role that 2E gave us; The Stewards. They protect Creation from the Fair Folk and other unsavory otherworldly creatures. The Lunars with their ability to learn FF charms and the anima abilities of the original five castes suited them to combat the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> I think this next bit is my headcanon, so just a head's up. When the gods were planning the War, the gods reasoned the Primordials may become so desperate that they might invite the Fair Folk into Creation. The Primordials could defeat the Fair Folk, they've done so many times before, and undo the damage to Creation wrought by the fey. So the Lunars were designed to be able to become whatever they needed to be in order to defeat what ever the Wyld dreamt up.<br /> <br /> The Lunar design plan paid off. The Primordials realized that they had underestimated the Exalted and invited the Fair Folk into Creation. However, the gods, the Lunars and the Exalted under their command were able to defend Creation's borders. This allowed the Solars and their armies to stay focused on laying low the Primordials.<br /> <br /> In the Second Age, the role of the Lunars hasn't really changed much. They consider themselves the defenders of Creation's borders although of course they lack the First Age and even Time of Glory infrastructure and teamwork that allowed them to do so nearly flawlessly. Additionally the Underworld is making moves in diverse places in Creation. The appearance of these &quot;Deathlords&quot; with their Abyssal Exalted and the spreading of shadowlands is cause for concern for the already stretched too thin Stewards.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T23:17:48-08:00","id":999589,"title":"","content":"I think the precise reason they ditched that was because of how it encourages them to stick around Creation's borders instead of actually doing anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:07:20-08:00","id":999642,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no offense, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar362_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"362\" data-vbnamecard=\"362\">Darkon</a>, but I'm done being expected to play bouncer for the Fair Folk solely because of my splat type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-07-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:23:02-08:00","id":999648,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Lunars and their First Age role, I think in the past we've tended to reject the basic premise given in the original First Edition, of them being rulers of the &quot;Night Realm&quot; of the First Age, because of too much overlap with Night Castes and Eclipse Caste.<br /> <br /> I think that might be overthinking it a bit too much, and overstressing that there was no need for Lunars in this role due to &quot;Solar supremacy&quot;. We're OK still seeing plenty of space for Sidereals as advisors and decision making viziers in the Old Realm, despite the fact that you have Twilights and Eclipses whose thing is dabbling in dealing with spirits, and getting to the bottom of mysteries, and who are Very Smart about making decisions, and so you could argue they don't *need* Sidereals. So is there a difference?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar362_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"362\" data-vbnamecard=\"362\">Darkon</a>, I don't think that's a totally bad option, but if you embraced the spirit of that dichotomy where Lunars were focused on the Fair Folk and Solars on the Primordials, and gave Solars a lot of stuff that helped them deal with demons, learn demon magic and anti-demon magic, specifically, that other splats didn't get, then would that be good for them? Not purely rhetorical, I don't know - could be awesome, but seems like, yeah, you would have lots of stories crop up where demons are getting in everyone's business and Solars are going to hell to fight demons and the like, and then would you want that focus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 11-07-2016, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T04:24:06-08:00","id":999664,"title":"","content":"I think it's apparent from some developer comments that the role of the Lunar and the nature of the Lunar are distinct, but somewhat related.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat is, the nature of the Lunar is mutable, so the role of the Lunar has been <u>different things at different times</u>.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the Primordial War, let's say the role of the Lunar was to be the fierce seconds of the Solars, either alongside them or apart from them being powerful companions and delegates.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the Realm, the role of the Lunars was to be its guardians from a variety of threats, within and without. Not as a thing that Lunars are exclusively qualified for, it's just what they dedicated their power to in a different Age of the world, one less defined by a grandiose war.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the Second Age, the role of the Lunar is to be perennial survivors in the face of extreme opposition, and saboteurs of the architects of that opposition.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's an idea of this mutability expressed in a change in their Castes. It may also be in a change in their powers, but I'd say we'd have to wait and see on that; I would think such a thing would be more sensible as an impression of how their powers develop and interact, rather than outright different Charms, but who knows.<br /> <br /> \u200bUnder the circumstances, I would say that it's foolish to try and start with what the Lunars are like in the game and extrapolate them all the way back to their origins (and that trying to find them a place in the Primordial War in terms of a specific strategic or logistic niche to be given, rather than &quot;Luna was in on the whole thing as well, so throw her champions into the mix&quot; is the wrong way to approach that bit of backstory in the first place). At the same time, I think it might help to break away from the idea that what Lunars do in the setting and play needs to be something highly distinct, considering the possibility for unique ways of playing them.<br /> <br /> So, disregarding the Silver Pact (which the corebook is remarkably explicit on many Lunars doing, for all that people overlook it entirely), nothing about Lunars especially impedes or informs them doing things like living lives of adventure and intrigue.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the idea of a &quot;Night Realm&quot;... you know, that's the kind of thing that I would have been down on in the past, but in the spirit of my current ethos of &quot;approach 'canon' as something flexible and imperfect even in diegesis&quot;, I could accommodate the idea that the whole idea of a distinction in government based on what time of the day it is emerges from the First Age being recalled imperfectly and with an emphasis on mythology in the timespan that the game takes place in, which would attribute the half-remembered actions of the Lunars to some kind of mythic Realm of the night, rather than being a literal statement on the idea that every Solar tucked into bed at sundown and society fundamentally transformed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:46:15-08:00","id":999842,"title":"","content":"I apologize for not making my post more clear. I am often pressed for time and my posts/suggestions can come across as lacking flexibility. I meant to convey that the Lunars may have had a more defined role in the FA than in the present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=999589#post999589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the precise reason they ditched that was because of how it encourages them to stick around Creation's borders instead of actually doing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have stated that was the role in the FA; to protect Creation's borders from the FF and hunt down demon incursions in Creation. Now that assigned roles from the Solar Deliberative are long gone, Lunars have evolved to do whatever they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=999642#post999642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no offense, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar362_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"362\" data-vbnamecard=\"362\">Darkon</a>, but I'm done being expected to play bouncer for the Fair Folk solely because of my splat type.</div> </div> </div> </div>None taken. Straight-jacketing Exalt types into narrowly focused roles greatly limits options of fun. Like I said above, I should have been more clear. In the FA I imagined the Lunars being Creation's Stewards against the FF and demonic incursions. In the 2nd Age, their roles have evolved. They can continue to defend Creation's borders, they can continue to hunt down demonic incursions, and now they can infiltrate and eliminate shadowlands oftentimes further in Creation's interior. Additionally they can do whatever they like or none of it all. I once read a fanfiction short story about a Lunar who was running a criminal syndicate in the Imperial City. I thought it was a clever and fun idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=999648#post999648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar362_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"362\" data-vbnamecard=\"362\">Darkon</a>, I don't think that's a totally bad option, but if you embraced the spirit of that dichotomy where Lunars were focused on the Fair Folk and Solars on the Primordials, and gave Solars a lot of stuff that helped them deal with demons, learn demon magic and anti-demon magic, specifically, that other splats didn't get, then would that be good for them? Not purely rhetorical, I don't know - could be awesome, but seems like, yeah, you would have lots of stories crop up where demons are getting in everyone's business and Solars are going to hell to fight demons and the like, and then would you want that focus?</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake was making my statement appear as a dichotomy in the first place. I didn't mean to convey that each Exalt type was given an area of specific focus particularly in the 2nd Age. That's my mistake for posting in haste (which I frequently do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). In the Time of Tumult, Lunar anima abilities have changed giving them even more flexibility to adapt to whatever roles they desire.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:39:00-08:00","id":999989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=999842#post999842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize for not making my post more clear. I am often pressed for time and my posts/suggestions can come across as lacking flexibility. I meant to convey that the Lunars may have had a more defined role in the FA than in the present.<br /> <br /> I should have stated that was the role in the FA; to protect Creation's borders from the FF and hunt down demon incursions in Creation. Now that assigned roles from the Solar Deliberative are long gone, Lunars have evolved to do whatever they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything doing border-guarding in Creation is going to be in for a long stretch of finding nothing where they are, with hordes skipping through the vast area that the defenders in question can't cover when not there. Not really a gripping hook for anyone, that. Dragon-Blooded would have more success at it, given their substantially greater numbers, but when you get right down to it, you'd have to have mortal scouts riding around at some point, and even then, really only around where they live. There's just too much to monitor to have single individuals be entrusted with said duty and expect them to have any degree of success in the process.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:54:18-08:00","id":1000019,"title":"","content":"Well, supposing that Lunars being guardians of the Realm included having a duty at the vanguard of defence against the Wyld:<br /> <br /> \u200bI recall, way back when, back when there was an idea that Lunars would be fixed through errata, that our current developers came up with a Charm that would empower them in serving as a key defensive point against an incursion to an area, that was intended to synergize with Charms for possession and awareness of a territory. It all culminated in the idea of a Charm to have some stake of ownership of the territory of one's Solar, with the end result being that any hostile entity walking into Creation would come to the attention of at least one Lunar, who would immediately start building up strength to see them off.<br /> <br /> \u200bObviously not all concepts transition, but I would find there could still be some basis for them being forewarned without requiring delegation to another. If nothing else, the basic concept is not unfamiliar.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomething analogous to the shark that smells blood in the water over a distance of miles; that a sufficiently fine-tuned Lunar might taste that coppery sensation of something wandering where it doesn't belong, or hearing a discordant note in the songlines, and it calls them to hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:39:58-08:00","id":1000070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1000019#post1000019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSomething analogous to the shark that smells blood in the water over a distance of miles; that a sufficiently fine-tuned Lunar might taste that coppery sensation of something wandering where it doesn't belong, or hearing a discordant note in the songlines, and it calls them to hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't overlook the thrashing about in the water for that. In real life, there are corridors of cold water in the ocean that can deliver sounds clearer and from further away; when they do come from miles away, it might be that they heard something rather than smelling it. Interesting to wonder if a similar setup exists in the oceans of Exalted, since it might be one of the few occasions in which someone could manage to just sit somewhere and catch a disturbance (not in progress of course, but it would come to their ears).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T08:46:09-08:00","id":1000287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1000019#post1000019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, supposing that Lunars being guardians of the Realm included having a duty at the vanguard of defence against the Wyld:<br /> <br /> \u200bI recall, way back when, back when there was an idea that Lunars would be fixed through errata, that our current developers came up with a Charm that would empower them in serving as a key defensive point against an incursion to an area, that was intended to synergize with Charms for possession and awareness of a territory. It all culminated in the idea of a Charm to have some stake of ownership of the territory of one's Solar, with the end result being that any hostile entity walking into Creation would come to the attention of at least one Lunar, who would immediately start building up strength to see them off.<br /> <br /> \u200bObviously not all concepts transition, but I would find there could still be some basis for them being forewarned without requiring delegation to another. If nothing else, the basic concept is not unfamiliar.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomething analogous to the shark that smells blood in the water over a distance of miles; that a sufficiently fine-tuned Lunar might taste that coppery sensation of something wandering where it doesn't belong, or hearing a discordant note in the songlines, and it calls them to hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is a songline again? I can't recall the term from any of the 2E books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:33:12-08:00","id":1000466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1000287#post1000287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly is a songline again? I can't recall the term from any of the 2E books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mentioned in 1e, which assumed that you were <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songline\" target=\"_blank\">familiar with anthropology</a> for one reason or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:52:59-08:00","id":1000522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1000287#post1000287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly is a songline again?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm not really using it as an in-game technical term here, just an image for what might convey extrasensory information to a Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1000466#post1000466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was mentioned in 1e, which assumed that you were <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songline\" target=\"_blank\">familiar with anthropology</a> for one reason or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI could have sworn that I've heard accounts of the original book actually having and describing an in-setting form of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T17:03:12-08:00","id":1000533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1000522#post1000522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI could have sworn that I've heard accounts of the original book actually having and describing an in-setting form of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back, yes. Page 20 of Exalted: the Lunars (not to be confused with MoeP: Lunars), which describes them as mnemonic devices used to recount important mythic and historical details and reckon between landmarks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T17:11:55-08:00","id":1007494,"title":"","content":"So, reading some of the earlier 5 pages of this thread, someone suggested a re-write of the Lunar's fluff got me to thinking to a re-write to the whole setting of my own:<br /> <br /> So, changes:<br /> <br /> <i>Both</i> the Lunars and Solars absolutely vanish from Creation come the Usurpation. [2e: Not only do the Sidereals manage to lock up most of the Solars shards into the Jade Prison, but they contrive a means to get the Lunar shards to dick off into the Wyld, for like, ever. / 3e: When Sol Invictus turned his face from Creation in shame, Luna lost interest herself, a bit fed up with this bullshit too.] [2e: When the Jade Prison broke, it lit up like a beacon across Everything, and led the Lunar shards slowly back to Creation. / 3e: When Sol finally turned his favor back to Creation, Luna's attention began to wax back as well.]<br /> <br /> The Solars returned all in one go. It was just <i>bam</i>, Solars are back. [2e-ish: Not only that, their return reawakened a few Eldar Solars from suspended animation, who fled into a deep sleep hidden from the gaze of Fate. With the Solars returning, they're interested in getting the world back on track with the help of all these younglings. To aid them, they've reactivated old dormant infrastructures that they had left behind, but remain functioning, such as cults or somesuch, after countless generations, awaiting the return of their lord, ancient arsenals hidden beneath the earth or old pacts that even now hold water.] Lunars have been trickling in, one by one, their coming unnoticed, unheralded. Unlike the Solars, they've been largely forgotten, not even remembered in twisted tales of Immaculate propaganda. They're god-blooded or something as far as anyone else is concerned. [2e-ish: And Elder Lunars have followed the beacon back as well after their long banishment to the Wyld. They don't have any infrastructure, but they're singular power houses all on their own.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:32:28-08:00","id":1026141,"title":"","content":"Reposting some thoughts I had on Lunar Exalted before the release of 3rd Edition:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've been thinking that the Lunar Exalted may be intended to cater to a specific human fantasy: To let loose.<br /> <br /> But true to the themes of the game, it's also about the consequences others have to face when you have the power to let loose and get away with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars don't have Socialize or Bureaucracy magic. Nothing which allows them to exert fine control over a society or organization of great size and complicated structure. They can make big impacts, but those impacts are rough and destabilizing.<br /> <br /> The more that the Moon-Beasts find themselves surrounded by such things, the more they need to act with care, and the more power other Exalted can bring to bear against them.<br /> <br /> But if Lunar Exalted can cause trouble carelessly, they can cause even more damage deliberately. They are perhaps uniquely suited for tearing apart order and introducing chaos, as well as being uniquely suited for thriving within sudden chaos.<br /> <br /> The question is: Do you care for all of the little people who can't handle it?<br /> <br /> A Lunar within a Solar's kingdom must decide if he cares whether or not the waves he makes will capsize the mortals around him.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those were my thoughts before learning about the new Lunar focus on &quot;freedom&quot;, but I think that &quot;to let loose (destructively)&quot; certainly fits.<br /> <br /> At any time, a Lunar trapped in a net and sinking into the waters can transform into an enormous whale. He breaks free of the ropes and becomes at home in the sea, but the sudden displacement of water caused by his new mass threatens to capsize the mortals around him. Is that what he wants, or does he need to restrain his full might because he cares about them?<br /> <br /> If Lunar Charms capitalize on that idea of &quot;my full power is dangerous for those around me&quot;, then it brings an internal tension to the Lunar narrative of freedom. The Lunar must always be asking himself how much his personal freedom is worth, and how many restrictions he is willing to accept for infrastructural support and the assistance of allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:13:19-08:00","id":1026203,"title":"","content":"That might be at odds with the stated desire to not turn the Lunar narrative into a wolfman story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:26:13-08:00","id":1026212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1026203#post1026203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be at odds with the stated desire to not turn the Lunar narrative into a wolfman story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wolfman story was about Horror Hunger and losing control of homicidally violent urges. Not about having a power you could deliberately use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:59:21-08:00","id":1026225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1026212#post1026212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wolfman story was about Horror Hunger and losing control of homicidally violent urges. Not about having a power you could deliberately use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted. The other objection would be that it still doesn't necessarily seem completely inherent or a solely Lunar thing, since some other Exalted might happen to have similar issues with that. Infernals caused peoples' faces to melt off with Demon Emperor Shintai, for example, while Alchemicals eventually become huge engines of war that can't get any smaller than a warstrider, and the rules for warstriders painted a picture of collateral damage like nothing else, since anything a strider just accidentally brushed by suffered a feat of strength/demolition attempt with half the warstrider's Strength + the character's Athletics total (probably a lot more in EX3, since they're billed as super-type robots). Pilots that are being exceedingly careful would still likely end up breaking a few buildings. Even Dragon-Blooded have anima flux to worry about, as well as damaging auras as a consequence of burning all incoming arrows into harmless sprays of cinders and ash; the mere existence of anima flux is explicitly why the Realm builds almost entirely with stone and not wood.<br /> <br /> Out of all of those, I'd say that Lunars may be the most comfortable with cutting loose and most able to avoid widespread damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:50:07-08:00","id":1026263,"title":"","content":"Having looked back at the core write-up for the Dragon Blooded, I wonder if they might build off of Anima Flux now and make the idea that their Elemental Essence is a wild, dangerous thing that needs to be tamed evident throughout more of their powers.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe idea that there can be something dangerously unrestrained about Lunars feels as though it may be fitting to how they're currently being written and how the developers have referenced them for years, but I think it would need to rest on something more substantive than the volume displacement incurred by turning into something large.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt might be something that comes through in their version of the Great Curse. Wyld Taint and Second Edition chimerism had issues, but I think there could have still been potential in the idea of getting Limit from your own powers.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know First Edition didn't have the same kinds of chimeras, but did it still have something to the tattoos besides fixing one's Caste? I think that even without chimerism, there might be something to the tattoos helping to stabilise their tumultuous personalities this run around, given a couple of things Holden has said.<br /> <br /> \u200bPart of what I thought was wasted potential in Wyld Taint was that it was wholly irrelevant to most playable characters, so I think and would like the results of a similar thing to be muted even with the tattoos. Something like the untattooed Lunar risking Limit for a broader use of powers and perhaps indulgences in Intimacies, whereas the Lunar with tattoos restricts this to only particular uses of power or other Intimate activity. You get caught in a net and have a number of choices for how to escape, but choosing the big, flashy, violent one nets you a bit of Limit, all building up to a Break which is less refined than that of Solars. Possibly Bonding themselves to something (Solars, the destruction of the Realm, some personal cause) could interact with this, although I couldn't say if it would be to create an avenue safe from ever building up Limit or that provides a means of losing it or even just being the focused target of it (i.e. whatever might cause you to Limit Break, your fury is directed at the Realm).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:53:13-08:00","id":1026264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-State</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar#post971950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you guys think?<br /> Sorry for the length</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is roughly like my thinking. Solars, with their Supernal Abilities in 3rd Edition are designed to be peerless in whatever they specialize in - Lunars in contrast may have been the original Exalted Host's ultimate generalists, infinitely adaptable to any situation.<br /> <br /> Of course Solars can make amazing generalists, and Lunars can be incredible in something they choose to focus on specializing in - but it's not what they're mechanics make them respectively best at doing.<br /> <br /> If Lunars have some special mechanic ala Solars having Supernal Abilities, perhaps it could be something like the ability to temporarily assume the power of a charm they qualify for but do not possess, thus letting &quot;shift&quot; to adapt themselves to a situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> In 2nd Edition the best I came up with was that Lunars had the twin opposing purposes of &quot;Stewards&quot; and &quot;Iconoclasts&quot; in specific reflection of Luna's nature as the <i><b>Fickle Lady. </b></i>In 3rd Edition this could actually be reflected in a cool way in their mechanics rather than just being a fluff concept to justify their relative lack of theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> (complimenting the Solar &amp; Lunar shticks, Dragon-Blooded would hypothetically be all about being greater than the sum of their numbers, via stacking their power together exponentially in ways other Exalted can't; and Sidereals are about being weird)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-03-2017, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T12:02:36-08:00","id":1026642,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the shapeshifting itself might be sufficient to constitute the Lunar &quot;equivalent&quot; to Supernal Ability, considering how much the developers have emphasized that it forms a means of getting useful abilities that don't have to fit with your character concept or require a lot of development and does not cost XP.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, here's a proposition that's bound to be unpopular: the idea that the end game of the Silver Pact, of a world in which the Lunars have eradicated the Realm and the strength of the Sidereals (and, from the point after the Solars return) and become truly free, and the role that they would acquire under such circumstances, would be a terrible disaster and is one of the things that the return of the Solars is intended to... how can I put this in a neutral manner... have an effect on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T13:54:31-08:00","id":1026673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1026642#post1026642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the shapeshifting itself might be sufficient to constitute the Lunar &quot;equivalent&quot; to Supernal Ability, considering how much the developers have emphasized that it forms a means of getting useful abilities that don't have to fit with your character concept or require a lot of development and does not cost XP.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, here's a proposition that's bound to be unpopular: the idea that the end game of the Silver Pact, of a world in which the Lunars have eradicated the Realm and the strength of the Sidereals (and, from the point after the Solars return) and become truly free, and the role that they would acquire under such circumstances, would be a terrible disaster and is one of the things that the return of the Solars is intended to... how can I put this in a neutral manner... have an effect on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I must say, the little tidbit in the 3E Corebook about Lunars basically strong-arming &quot;barbarians&quot; into mass-suicide rushes against the Realm made me ...... uncomfortable. Like, <i>really</i> uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Coming from someone who's &quot;favorite&quot; splat was the Lunars, and from someone who enjoyed the basic premise of the Thousand-Streams-River, that means a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:18:47-08:00","id":1049835,"title":"","content":"Lunars are my favorite splat as well, setting and story wise at least. <br /> <br /> I think that Lunar storytelling can benefit from two ideas. <br /> <br /> First, is that of the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Deuteragonist\" target=\"_blank\">deuteragonist</a> role in a story. Not to say second-fiddle (second-fiddle storytelling really chaps my backside, no matter the setting), but as the heroes whose heroic journey takes them into a variety of set-piece situations. They resolve the situation and the story arc by becoming part of it - making it also their own - and finding the solution from within.<br /> <br /> For example, a Lunar Pack might travel to an area beset by strife among several factions. Where a Solar Circle might find direct opposition to themselves and their own goals, the Pack would use Charms and Influence to adapt into the conflict and it's participants. The Pack's resolution of the conflict would have them as the ones who move the story and are the focus of the story, but the story arc remains &quot;about&quot; the set-piece conflict. <br /> <br /> I suspect a lot of stories take this shape naturally, anyway! The trick would be to keep from turning the heroes into mere spectators or sidekicks.<br /> <br /> The other idea that seems very Lunar to me is to focus on being rather than doing. (See <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Dramatica\" target=\"_blank\">this page</a> , about 1/3 down, regarding personal style) <br /> <br /> The Lunar adapts to the environment, to the scene, to the story, to the conflict. At each story arc, the Lunar *agonist becomes something more than he had been before. <br /> <br /> In a story arc where a Solar would go to discover a secret of world-shaking sorcery to complete the story (perhaps to destroy an army or to lift a vast curse), the Lunar would go to hunt and eat that secret. The Solar's climactic scene would be to cast the spell, while the Lunar's climactic scene would be to <i>become</i> the spell, hurling <i>themselves</i> into the army or into the dark heart of the curse.<br /> <br /> The Solar hero rides away (sometimes <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Hero_Rides_Away\" target=\"_blank\">literally</a>), leaving behind tales of their glory. The Lunar hero <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/396213-on-moonsilver-tattoos-in-3rd-ed\">carries forever</a> the tales and glories that they've accumulated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just my Resources (**)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:24:52-08:00","id":1050020,"title":"","content":"I don't know how well this holds up, but it seemed to me that one interpretation of 2e lunars' role was &quot;begin as an outcast from society, reshape the society until you aren't anymore&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T16:15:23-08:00","id":1050132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1026264#post1026264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 2nd Edition the best I came up with was that Lunars had the twin opposing purposes of &quot;Stewards&quot; and &quot;Iconoclasts&quot; in specific reflection of Luna's nature as the <i><b>Fickle Lady. </b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than Limit Breaking as we know it, it would be interesting if the Lunars actually shifted between the Steward and Iconoclast fixations as they moved along their &quot;limit track&quot;. When empty (full moon) they are fixated on their stewardship of their positive intimacies, but as their limit fills those intimacies dry up and they are only able to focus upon negative intimacies (intimacies ignored in their steward phase). This would certainly help RP and encapsulate the fickle nature of Lunars and draw them further from Solars (a good thing imo). The creator and the destroyer - Vishnu and Shiva in turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","user":"Touch_of_Sepia","date":". 02-16-2017, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:00:33-08:00","id":1050188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1050132#post1050132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather than Limit Breaking as we know it, it would be interesting if the Lunars actually shifted between the Steward and Iconoclast fixations as they moved along their &amp;quot;limit track&amp;quot;. When empty (full moon) they are fixated on their stewardship of their positive intimacies, but as their limit fills those intimacies dry up and they are only able to focus upon negative intimacies (intimacies ignored in their steward phase). This would certainly help RP and encapsulate the fickle nature of Lunars and draw them further from Solars (a good thing imo). The creator and the destroyer - Vishnu and Shiva in turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1 because I like the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T20:10:03-08:00","id":1050276,"title":"","content":"I think there's a bit where for me at least, Lunars should have an air of violence or savagery to me. I think <i>that's</i> the big thing to be drawn from the werewolf motifs they have. It's the theme I feel that most unites the two Werewolf games produced by White Wolf more than anything else at least. And to me, Lunars when you read their 1e corebook write-up have this sort of energy to them (for me at least). Solars ruled by day. Lunars ruled by night. Solars made shining cities where those who bought into the system got utopia. Lunars made pyramid skulls of the people who didn't.<br /> <br /> 3e's take on this to me feels to be expanding this. Lunars were the second from the top in th eold order. They helped fuel the Usurpation by their positions as Second and in a very violent, dark and often scary sort of Second. They had to be hunted with the Solars because taking out the Solars took their power base and they were the guys closest to the boss. It's like how in real world coups you have to often purge the loyalists. Because when you want to be in cahrge, the guys who had the most to lose from you being in charge are the most dangerous.<br /> <br /> To me this makes Lunars in 3e insurgents. It's just kind of on a weird, global scale. The throne of the world is to many elder Lunar Exalted <i>theirs</i>. It was stolen from them by backstabbing Sidereals and usurping Terrestrails. They are pushed to the edges of relevance in the center of the world and also labeled enemies by that Center now. The Lunar war on the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals is a rejection fo the hegemony which chose to eject them from the table preemptively. And they are an Exalt sort who even before that were probably characterized by aspects of darkness, predation, the night and violence. <br /> <br /> To me, 2e Lunars were written a bit trying to run from what 1e Lunars were without asking what was the first principles. And a lot of spin-offs from there have progressively resulted in something that's basically not even what the 1e thing was at all. And it feels like 3e is trying to get back to that. Which is fine by me I guess. I like the idea of an Exalt who focuses on the less savery nature of nature, run on a basic idea that &quot;Hobbes was right, Rousseau was wrong&quot; and to some extent show that your &quot;heroic resistance&quot; in a lot of fantasy settings could easily just be a bunch of savages at the gate who want the throne for themselves.<br /> <br /> Plus, less playing at society-making is nice since well, 2e implied a lot of it was futile (sinc ethe Realm eats them), a lot of it was kind of built on unearned taking of setting elements (because 2e liked not making new things up) and also makes it so the entire Lunar premise is &quot;We don't need you dad!&quot; to Solars and then suddenly having Solars showing up and out-doing htem at everything they were doing ever. Having it be an insurgency that they have done significant damage already, which they can rule in when their enemies can't and which allows for young opportunistic Lunars personal glory and power (since well, let's be honest, most young Lunars are enough normal of people to think that's fine by them) in the process well...power and glory. It's a very cynical, mean and realpolitik bit of cultural heroism I think. But I like pragmatic realism over utopianism anyhow.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not like the most famous utopia books are all that hot anyhow. (The Republic seems very much like a society Lunars would build. It's also a caste-based information-controlling dicatorship.)<br /> <br /> And stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:21:24-08:00","id":1050513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1050188#post1050188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> +1 because I like the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In First Age Terms, the Lunar and Solar rule a territory as a pair, common practice. Much of the time the Lunar is &quot;home&quot; tending the Dragonblooded Gens, shepherding and grooming the territory, and tending with great love to whatever children/projects may exist. Over time, the stress of high society and court (visiting lunars in their pissed phase) drives them towards their negative intimacies - going on aggressive diplomatic missions as lord and representative of their nation, undermining or sabotaging rival states, leading armies into the Wlyd and otherwise tearing down and attacking anything they have beef with. Now, they are a contributing factor to the failings of Solar governance, rather than passive standers by - much cooler and better fit to what others would perceive as a fickle nature.<br /> <br /> In the Second Age, the Elders being far more in the throws of their curse, they are given over to their negative intimacies far more often than their positive. Rarely building anything that they love - only working towards things that they hate. Roxxy, her hate of humanity and the civilization that so ruined her life, is stuck in a constant cycle of debauchery and consumption of her hatreds, making no progress towards her love of sorcery despite all the tools and resources before her. Maha does not build his army because he loves it, but is stuck working towards throwing down the Dragonbloods who he blames for stealing his perfect life, unable to follow his positive intimacies towards romance or love of self to any real degree. This does a great deal to explain why Lunar Elders have done so little constructive work in the last 700 odd years. They can no longer build anything constructive, though they remember how. The terror it fills me with to have your loves wither, to be consumed by your hatred... the true Alpha Predator is the growing hate in every Lunars heart, for it will one day consume the Lunars themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","user":"Touch_of_Sepia","date":".  Adding more to the post. 02-17-2017, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:59:32-08:00","id":1050559,"title":"","content":"That's all very... neat, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T11:31:08-08:00","id":1050612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1050559#post1050559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's all very... neat, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've no idea Isator Levi.<br /> <br /> <i>(Checks the thread title, yup, 'What is the role of the Lunar'. Post fits the topic.)</i><br /> <br /> I will say that's a pretty pointless post and I'm not sure if it's a shit post or not, but tone is never a known quantity in the medium. I won't preach any further on that, what with your 10,000+ posts and what not.<br /> <br /> <u>I will bring this back around to something worth reading/skimming:</u><br /> <br /> I've been thinking around how Solars represent the shattered glass ceiling of skill, the mandate of rulership, and perfection. I would not say rulership is intrinsic to their essence - only a mandate handed down to them like a title or reward. This leaves perfection and skill taken to 11. The Solars concept of perfection is important as it is double edged: it allows them to make perfect solutions crafted to each independent problem, it also (should) prevent them from having powers or charms that grant overmuch flexibility as that would not be the perfect solution to *the* problem. Given a hundred years in a world allowed to change or any number (infinite) of other shifting variables, that perfect solution is no longer viable for the much changed problem. I think this would be a far better flaw for the Solars - their perfection is their own downfall. Much akin to the UCS who can not turn his back on his perfect valor/compassion, the UCS who can not hold back the benediction of his blessings to the point where a prayer for light and good weather results in sun scorched crops or compassion so potent that no side can be taken without full knowledge of the infinite repercussions that will result down the stream of time for any particular action... perfection is a difficult maxim to live up to, even if it does allow all doors to be open and all hurtles jumped. Perfection is subjective based on the problem, person and situation - the inflexible Solar constantly forced to build anew or relentlessly maintain the constants that allowed their first great experiment.<br /> <br /> Solars have been allowed to be far far far too flexible and this has made it impossible to define the Lunar as flexible when compared to the Solar. We say it all the time and point to Attribute vs Ability, but really it's a very thin argument. We point to Solars and preach that their should be no flaw, that they are perfect, but perfection is a flaw. I think if we rounded out Solars better it would give depth to all of the other splats. Right now, with Solars being everything - it just white washes the world into Solars and those guys with power x that are not as good as Solars. For a Storyteller game, that's pretty weak. It gives little credence to why people would rebel against them, well, perfection can be stagnation or the tearing up of huge works/peoples/civilizations to lay down the next perfect solution to a changing world.<br /> <br /> Given such a focus on the hidebound inflexibility of the Solars perfection - the fickle and enforced flexibility of the Lunars own curse/personality would be much richer. The best solution is the all inclusive one, where all of the Exalts Boons/Flaws and all, are made in such a way as to highlight the others...rather than throw shade upon or wash out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","user":"Touch_of_Sepia","date":". 02-17-2017, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T13:14:44-08:00","id":1050674,"title":"","content":"I got what Isator meant. It was a valid point. I don't think he was shit-posting.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> People always seem very intent on finding a role for Lunars, a job for them to do (I must have seen tons of threads about it over the years), and honestly, I think it's a waste of time.<br /> <br /> The role of Lunars isn't to be Solars number 2s, or adaptable heroes, or something like that.<br /> Their role is to be awesome monster-heroes who turn into loads of awesome animals. Their role is to be a character that's more fun to play than a Solar if you like having a whole toolbox of weird tricks to adapt, but not to the extent of a Sidereal. Their role is to get to turn into a giant monster. Their role is to be a savage barbarian out to save the world from an evil Empire.<br /> What I mean is, Lunars have powers and themes and so on, but they don't need a role in the world pre-determined for them by some cosmic designer, because their role in the game is to be the bestial antiheroes who lurk at the edge of the world, and that's far more important.<br /> <br /> Who cares what the Gods designed them for? Sure, maybe the fluff can mention that, maybe not (Luna's mad, maybe she had no real plan for them, or maybe this is just what you naturally get when you make a Luna-based Exalt).<br /> <br /> For example, the OP said:<br /> &quot;Solars-rulers, god kings of creation. They represent perfection.<br /> Sidereal- advisers and teachers of the exalted. They guide the world fate in the background<br /> Dragon Blooded- Soldiers of creation. They control the elements them self.&quot;<br /> <br /> These are all fine. But Solars don't have to be rulers. That's what they did in the 1st age, and it's what some do now (like the Bull), but most Solars actually aren't kings now. I mean, your average Night PC is an awesome thief-hero, not a ruler.<br /> Dragon-blood don't have to be the soldiers of Creation. They were in the first age; now they're the aristocratic imperialists who oppress Creation. Some are soldiers, some are politicians, some are sorcerers, whatever.<br /> Sidereals? Well, Sidereals do have an advising and teaching theme, but it's actually not a big one, because most Sidereal games do not revolve around teaching Exalts, they revolve about you, the Sidereal agent of Heaven, saving reality from existential threats.<br /> <br /> So, why do Lunars need some preset role in the game-world?<br /> <br /> Look, if Dragonblood weren't the Soldiers of Creation in the Primordial War, it wouldn't be a big deal: they're still elemental-powered super-aristocrats, which is the main thing for them. I'm not saying get rid of the soldiers-of-creation thing; I'm saying it's not that big a theme. Similarly, Solars being rulers is actually not a big theme of them, because most Solars are not rulers. They're reincarnated rulers, sure, but in the 2nd age many of them are wandering heroes, because their primary role is to be player-accessible hero-characters.<br /> <br /> Lunars have had problems with theme before, often seeming like Silver Solars (with some charms that were just literal reprints of Solar charms). But I don't think the main issue was ever that they didn't have a strong &quot;role&quot; in the setting. I mean, Abyssals had a strong role in the setting (destroy the entire world) and many think that was a bad thing for Abyssals as a splat, and later in the edition writers tried to move away from it. Similarly with Infernals, whose role in the setting was to free the Yozis. Both of these were too restrictive, and drew attention away from the real point of them, which was to be death-themed villains/anti-heroes and Princes of Hell.<br /> Their role in the<i> game</i> is much more important than their role in the <i>setting</i>.<br /> <br /> I'll be frank: I've played a couple of Lunars, and so have several of my friends, they're almost as popular as Solars. And never have I heard anyone say &quot;I really wish their role in the setting's history was more defined.&quot; Nor did the people who haven't played them as much ever say &quot;I don't like Lunars because they lack a defined role.&quot; The only complaint I've heard about their role in the setting was that they wished they didn't have all that stuff about being No.2 to Solars.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T19:43:38-08:00","id":1050854,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it might've been less confusing if Isator had said &quot;tidy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T20:16:54-08:00","id":1050865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1050513#post1050513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In First Age Terms, the Lunar and Solar rule a territory as a pair, common practice. Much of the time the Lunar is &quot;home&quot; tending the Dragonblooded Gens, shepherding and grooming the territory, and tending with great love to whatever children/projects may exist. Over time, the stress of high society and court (visiting lunars in their pissed phase) drives them towards their negative intimacies - going on aggressive diplomatic missions as lord and representative of their nation, undermining or sabotaging rival states, leading armies into the Wlyd and otherwise tearing down and attacking anything they have beef with. Now, they are a contributing factor to the failings of Solar governance, rather than passive standers by - much cooler and better fit to what others would perceive as a fickle nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e, sure. Note that part of this thread is the inspiration of Lunars in 3e. And a good chunk of thise presupposes a few thing about the nature fo the Exalted, the First Age and such presente doriginally in <b>Dreams of the First Age</b> which are not the case in 3e's First Age or Creation at all. Solars and Lunars aren't guranteed to be paired and any pairings were likely a common trend but not required amongst pairings. There are more Lunars than Solars. Dragon-Blooded likely aren't greatly reduced in number such that a whole Lookshy's worth of DBs were serving every Solar. And the Wyld's very nature is likely different from what it was before.<br /> <br /> I think what Isator is mentioning is your take is a tad tidy for what they are implied to be in the 1e corebook and what likely the original dev notes talked about with them. See my points on savagery and violence. Solars had their neat kingdoms, caliphates and empires. Lunars were part of that regime, sometimes iwht personal ties to individual Solars. But they were their won rulers of the Night while Solars were rulers by Day. I think if there's any contrasting with Solars, it is that they were this uncontrolled force that helped play into the Solar regieme. THey complimented the Solar rule as a whole and as a force, rather than I feel soemthing every single Solar kingdom had as a co-ruler. There were too many Lunars and Solars themselves probably didnt' sturcture their domains in that fashion in 3e's take of the First Age (what little we'll see on that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1050513#post1050513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Second Age, the Elders being far more in the throws of their curse, they are given over to their negative intimacies far more often than their positive. Rarely building anything that they love - only working towards things that they hate. Roxxy, her hate of humanity and the civilization that so ruined her life, is stuck in a constant cycle of debauchery and consumption of her hatreds, making no progress towards her love of sorcery despite all the tools and resources before her. Maha does not build his army because he loves it, but is stuck working towards throwing down the Dragonbloods who he blames for stealing his perfect life, unable to follow his positive intimacies towards romance or love of self to any real degree. This does a great deal to explain why Lunar Elders have done so little constructive work in the last 700 odd years. They can no longer build anything constructive, though they remember how. The terror it fills me with to have your loves wither, to be consumed by your hatred... the true Alpha Predator is the growing hate in every Lunars heart, for it will one day consume the Lunars themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this feels a bit too &quot;idealistic&quot; to me on what I think Lunar motivations for 3e are presented. It's not the curse in itself that makes the elders angry and bitter. It's not some high brow view on the natuer of civilization, humanity or the Exalted. It's the world is, as they see it, their birthright, they've been robbed and pretenders sit on the throne of the world. Now at this poin thte war has gone so long that many elders probably have now end game. But I think you're overl emphasizing Intimacies as things which determine PC psychology. NPCs only ahve the Intimacies which matter for PC interaction. WHat matters for story stuff like the workings of Lunar elders I think should be couched more in strictly plot-based terms personally.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T02:04:10-08:00","id":1050918,"title":"","content":"What I meant was that I find it to be a take both on their Curse and their role that is very proscriptive and reductive, both in how it affects their personalities and their actions in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T03:50:49-08:00","id":1050936,"title":"","content":"Kinda reminds me of your post on <i>The Dark Knight</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:22:17-08:00","id":1051094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1050918#post1050918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was that I find it to be a take both on their Curse and their role that is very proscriptive and reductive, both in how it affects their personalities and their actions in history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you prefer the traditional reasoning that the Lunars have just sat on their hands for 800 years and done nothing? It's not even proscriptive as Rain Deathflyer and Silver Python have largely avoided the worst of the curse and built something. The Hislanti League as well was something Lunars have built despite the slippery slope of their own hatreds. Also Leviathan spends most of his time mopping about his dead positive intimacy and only rarely goes out to sink Realm boats, so he seems to have avoided it some as well. I mean I don't know about you, but I've seen a lot of bad players in my decade playing/running Exalted - any guides to proper in theme RP is a positive imo.<br /> <br /> Right now there is nothing fickle about Lunars that I've seen in official writing nor in player RP. The closest would be Lunars messing around as talking animals the majority of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:11:20-08:00","id":1051121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1051094#post1051094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you prefer the traditional reasoning that the Lunars have just sat on their hands for 800 years and done nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding the false dichotomy, the answer to this question depends on whether or not this is your read on how the Third Edition core presents them.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo address the false dichotomy: pointing out an issue I see in a proposed solution does not mean that I am saying that no solution is possible or necessary, just that I don't think the proposal works.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now there is nothing fickle about Lunars that I've seen in official writing nor in player RP.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bEven to the extent that I would agree that that specifically needs to be a thing, I think that the idea of incorporating it by giving them two highly defined base states that they switch back and forth between wouldn't be a very good way of depicting it.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut honestly, I don't think Lunars as a whole really need to be very fickle. As a trait of Luna, maybe it could be a motif that is alluded to in some way by certain powers, but otherwise it feels like a proscription on Lunars that is not really helpful.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can imagine that being fickle might have been part of the popular perception of Lunars back in the First Age, maybe a bit more of the characteristics present in those Chosen to be them or that emerges from their capabilities and place in the world during that mythic and peaceful era, but those days are gone.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not saying that it's absent entirely (I think I've once imagined it as being something that might come through in my proposal of a power in which they hone their mind towards destroying particular enemies), just that Lunars in survival mode are less playful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:32:03-08:00","id":1051126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1050612#post1050612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking around how Solars represent the shattered glass ceiling of skill, the mandate of rulership, and perfection. I would not say rulership is intrinsic to their essence - only a mandate handed down to them like a title or reward. This leaves perfection and skill taken to 11. The Solars concept of perfection is important as it is double edged: it allows them to make perfect solutions crafted to each independent problem, it also (should) prevent them from having powers or charms that grant overmuch flexibility as that would not be the perfect solution to *the* problem. Given a hundred years in a world allowed to change or any number (infinite) of other shifting variables, that perfect solution is no longer viable for the much changed problem. I think this would be a far better flaw for the Solars - their perfection is their own downfall. Much akin to the UCS who can not turn his back on his perfect valor/compassion, the UCS who can not hold back the benediction of his blessings to the point where a prayer for light and good weather results in sun scorched crops or compassion so potent that no side can be taken without full knowledge of the infinite repercussions that will result down the stream of time for any particular action... perfection is a difficult maxim to live up to, even if it does allow all doors to be open and all hurtles jumped. Perfection is subjective based on the problem, person and situation - the inflexible Solar constantly forced to build anew or relentlessly maintain the constants that allowed their first great experiment.<br /> <br /> <b>Solars have been allowed to be far far far too flexible and this has made it impossible to define the Lunar as flexible when compared to the Solar. We say it all the time and point to Attribute vs Ability, but really it's a very thin argument.</b> We point to Solars and preach that their should be no flaw, that they are perfect, but perfection is a flaw. I think if we rounded out Solars better it would give depth to all of the other splats. Right now, with Solars being everything - it just white washes the world into Solars and those guys with power x that are not as good as Solars. For a Storyteller game, that's pretty weak. It gives little credence to why people would rebel against them, well, perfection can be stagnation or the tearing up of huge works/peoples/civilizations to lay down the next perfect solution to a changing world.<br /> <br /> Given such a focus on the hidebound inflexibility of the Solars perfection - the fickle and enforced flexibility of the Lunars own curse/personality would be much richer. The best solution is the all inclusive one, where all of the Exalts Boons/Flaws and all, are made in such a way as to highlight the others...rather than throw shade upon or wash out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a good idea not define them as flexible compared to the Solars, because just saying the word flexible doesn't get across that they're bestial shapeshifters, which is their proper definition. Flexibility falls out of this, rather than being the primary goal in and of itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T15:28:43-08:00","id":1051182,"title":"","content":"I think some flexibility could be in Lunars, but distinct from how Solars do it. That Solars can be good at basically anything, so long as they actually develop in those things, while Lunars might have some smaller number of things that can be developed which can be applied to numerous things. As an illustration rather than suggestion, the idea that a Lunar could develop down one branch that can include good sword fighting in addition to several other activities, if not exactly as good as Solars.<br /> <br /> I think the priority there would still be making the experience of playing them feel different, rather than niche protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:55:48-08:00","id":1053510,"title":"","content":"A way my brother has described one important aspect of the roles of the Lunars in both 1e and 2e (don't know if 3e will be keeping it this way) was: whereas Solars are <i>mythical</i> heroes and <i>mythical</i> monsters and the Dragon Blooded are part of mortal society, Lunars are <i>folkloric</i> heroes and <i>folkloric</i> monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T20:43:59-08:00","id":1053612,"title":"","content":"That sounds a bit like a distinction without a difference to me.<br /> <br /> I'm sure it's the kind of thing I would have wondered about myself in the past, but if so it has ultimately led to the conclusion stated above.<br /> <br /> Hmm, role of the Lunar... shit, I had something for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T04:11:24-08:00","id":1053749,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this came out upthread already, I would certainly still expect the Lunar Charms to be focused and structured around activities, a la 2e Alchemicals, and not Abilities.<br /> <br /> So if you want to play a Lunar with combat focus, then there are tree(s) for combat which will let you do that, rather than sort of oblige you to go and buy Charms that have secondary functions outside of combat (or whatever activity of interest) that you're not interested in playing a character with, etc.<br /> <br /> But if you want to be a character who's like all &quot;Well, I'm great at combat, 'cos I have tons of Melee enhancing Charms, but very little in any other combat enhancing Ability, and it shows in how I fight and approach problems&quot; then Solars will still be your best bet, and Lunars won't really have much space for that.<br /> <br /> (Some activity focused trees will inevitably overlap with Ability based trees - Alchemicals 2e had a tree about survival, for instance, even though their trees are based around activities and challenges and not Abilities, because survival is an activity and a type of challenge equally as much as a capitalized Ability. In a way, yes, this is kind of on a theoretical level unsatisfying but I would think it's a necessary step to having characters that people actually want to play when rubber meets road.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T04:13:08-08:00","id":1053751,"title":"","content":"Oh, I remember now; it was about the idea that something closer to fickleness in Lunars could be found in the fact that they have no role, rather than in them periodically switching between two roles. I was thinking about how their current Castes are described not in terms of things that they do, but the manner in which they overcome obstacles and assert themselves against the world, and the idea that such a Lunar who can operate without constraints somewhere could cycle through a whole bunch of roles and ambitions in a manner that could be construed as fickleness.<br /> <br /> \u200bI wouldn't exactly define Solar Castes as inescapable or inflexible, but that there tends to be a consistency to them through means of the kinds of people the Unconquered Sun selects for them, and the feeling one gets from pursuing them. I could read the acquisition of Solars XP via Caste as representing the idea that Caste represents a role and purpose that is reliably spiritually fulfilling for a Solar, not as something that turns them into a stereotype, but as part of the basis for why a Solar might repeatedly engage in functions of the Caste over the centuries.<br /> <br /> \u200bI could see Lunars as getting things differently in a manner that means that some of them might frequently switch their interests.<br /> <br /> \u200bI have this idea of a Full Moon Lunar who started out in the far North living in her ruined mountain fortress manse, going out to get into fights with the local gods and elementals and Fair Folk and stronger, more aggressive tribes, then became a kind of wandering beggar warrior-for hire while travelling down along the length of Creation through the East, and finally wound up in... well, it was originally the South, but now I find the political situations of the Southeast to be more fitting, and she became a champion of a resistance movement within one of the empires and ultimately, after some encouragement from her son, who tracked her down for one of his visits every fifteen years or so, opted to try her hand as a monarch for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T05:34:07-08:00","id":1053768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1053749#post1053749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would certainly still expect the Lunar Charms to be focused and structured around activities, a la 2e Alchemicals, and not Abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well something that struck me about the way Alchemical Charms were organised there was that they basically weren't arranged by Attribute at all. That it went beyond just cascades that would occasionally branch through different Attributes and into the sole focus of their arrangement being on their utilities. It finally helped me make sense of their descriptions in the Wiki, I'll tell you that.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd it works for them because part of the concept they had there was that the Exalted could buy the Charms for cheap, and that even Attribute requirements could be handily fulfilled by Augmentations, and the limit was on how much of one's arsenal could be accessed at any given time. It's part of why I've considered that version of Alchemicals to not really even have Attribute Charms; Attributes work more than Abilities, or even just Essence, as the prerequisites, but a given Charm is expressing a concept other than the Attribute associated with it. Really, the expression of the whole Alchemical is coming through in something different from their Charms or traits, because those are things that can be modified with relative impunity.<br /> <br /> \u200bI may be biased by familiarity, but when I think of Lunar Charms, I still think that the expression of Attributes by them is important. I would think of a Lunar Strength Charm as an expression of strength, compared to an Alchemical one that is more a case of a given capability requiring a modification to this part of their makeup.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe fact that some Solar Charm cascades have been divided according to certain expressions or utilities would make me think that something like the Second Edition Lunar arrangement could still be the result, but I think that for something closer to the Alchemicals would entail a significant overhaul of them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not necessarily arguing against such an overhaul, I'm just laying out some of the premises that I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:11:29-08:00","id":1053778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1053751#post1053751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI have this idea of a Full Moon Lunar\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit, Isator, stop making me want to run games for you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (No, but seriously, I like your style, and I suspect you'd be nigh-invaluable as an ST's assistant.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:49:48-08:00","id":1053790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you want to play a Lunar with combat focus, then there are tree(s) for combat which will let you do that, rather than sort of oblige you to go and buy Charms that have secondary functions outside of combat (or whatever activity of interest) that you're not interested in playing a character with, etc. </div> </div> </div>I enjoy those kind of charms. They give you more to play with, more of a toolbox to solve problems with. Rather than &quot;I have to make Test X, so I use my Pass Test X charm&quot; which I find rather dull. It's why I enjoyed playing a Lunar, especially the shapechanging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:55:57-08:00","id":1053818,"title":"","content":"@ Isator, some stuff to think about here. I actually didn't know there was route whereby Alchemicals would buy Charm based Attribute increases that count as prerequisites, if I understand correctly, which I would presume are balanced by being cheaper in experience vs slots and committed essence?<br /> <br /> I think I see what you're talking about, and the Trait fluid Alchemicals might have gone further with their trees being application and situation based than an Attribute based Exalt without their assumptions might have. (With Alchemicals' really quite complicated and fluid recustomization minigame being much of the thing and Attributes being more of a workable constraint to hang this on than just hanging off Essence, or off Abilities). I could see the 3e mainly sticking to simple Attributes with each subtree having a focus on particular situations and uses, as I think seems to be the case for 2e. <br /> <br /> (What I would think might be a bad move would be the extreme of &quot;Next Strength Charm in the tree? Oh, spin the wheel of random functions that fall within Strength.&quot; or lots of general Charms that aren't specialised for any particular uses or situation at all, and so don't really interact with the mechanical systems in play very well. But this is an extreme.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1053790#post1053790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy those kind of charms. They give you more to play with, more of a toolbox to solve problems with. Rather than &quot;I have to make Test X, so I use my Pass Test X charm&quot; which I find rather dull. It's why I enjoyed playing a Lunar, especially the shapechanging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope for you then they'll have options for people with your preference and players who want to build a character that's been focused to beat specific challenges as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:19:52-08:00","id":1053976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/971950-the-role-of-the-lunar?p=1053818#post1053818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Isator, some stuff to think about here. I actually didn't know there was route whereby Alchemicals would buy Charm based Attribute increases that count as prerequisites</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes, the Fourth Attribute Augmentation. Has no prerequisites and minimums of Essence and Attribute 1, can be purchased for any Attribute, once purchased can be installed up to (Essence/2) times per Attribute, and you only need to commit Essence for the first installation, which costs one mote. It has the effect of increasing your Attribute cap by one and granting a free dot of the Attribute per installation. The Attribute boosts do not count towards your experience costs to raise Attributes, but count as your real value for all other purposes, including raising the cap for other Augmentations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">which I would presume are balanced by being cheaper in experience vs slots and committed essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bJust about. Alchemical paid (current rating) x 3 to raise Caste and Favoured Attributes, while all Charms cost a flat 6xp.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs far as I can see, there was also no limit to the number of Charm slots you could buy (with those also being cheap), and although this would typically gain diminishing returns if they outstripped your personal Essence pool, I could see somebody dedicating a few Charm slots just for this Augmentation considering how its commitment worked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}